WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:13.280
<v Ira Glass>When he wants to explain to people what his life is like these days, Lenny sometimes tells this story. On election night in 2016, he says he went to a bar, got a seat near a TV, ordered a beer, and started making small talk.
<v Ira Glass>当Lenny想向别人解释他如今的生活是什么样子时，他有时会讲这个故事。他说在2016年大选之夜，他走进一家酒吧，在电视机旁找了个座位，点了一杯啤酒，开始闲聊。

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:36.090
<v Lenny Pozner>And I turned to the guy to my right, and I said, "Did you vote"? And from there, he went into a long explanation about-- just some shadow government ideas, and whether voting makes a difference. And probably 10 minutes into it, he was talking about mass shootings, and then eventually Sandy Hook.
<v Lenny Pozner>我转向右边的那个人问：“你投票了吗？”从那以后，他就开始了一长篇大论——谈论一些影子政府的观点，以及投票到底有没有意义。大概谈了10分钟后，他开始谈论大规模枪击事件，最后谈到了桑迪胡克小学。

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:57.760
<v Ira Glass>Sandy Hook, of course, where a gunman killed 20 children, all in first grade, as well as seven adults. This random stranger then started telling Lenny this particular story about Sandy Hook. He thought the whole shooting was fake. It had to be fake, he said, because one of those first graders also showed up as a victim in a second mass shooting, all the way over in Pakistan.
<v Ira Glass>当然，桑迪胡克小学发生过一起枪击案，一名枪手杀害了20名一年级的孩子和7名成年人。这个陌生人随后开始向Lenny讲述关于桑迪胡克的特定故事。他说，他认为整场枪击案都是假的。他说那一定是假的，因为其中一名一年级学生竟然同时出现在巴基斯坦的另一起大规模枪击案中，成为受害者。

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:30.990
<v Ira Glass>In the corners of the internet where people trade Sandy Hook conspiracy stories, this is a key piece of evidence that Sandy Hook was not real. Of course, it was real. And what happened in Pakistan was, in reality, about two years after Sandy Hook. The Taliban gunned down more than 100 kids there. And there was a public vigil, and at the public vigil, probably as a sign of solidarity with other kids who had died in school shootings, mourners had this photo of a boy from Sandy Hook, smiling and wearing a Spider-Man shirt under a corduroy jacket with a furry collar.
<v Ira Glass>在互联网上那些传播桑迪胡克阴谋论的角落里，这是证明桑迪胡克是虚构的关键证据。当然，它是真实的。而巴基斯坦的那起事件，实际上发生在桑迪胡克事件大约两年后。塔利班在那里枪杀了100多名儿童。当时举行了公开守灵仪式，而在仪式上，哀悼者可能为了表示与在校园枪击案中遇难的其他孩子团结一致，手里拿着一张来自桑迪胡克的男孩的照片，男孩微笑着，穿着印有蜘蛛侠图案的衬衫，外面套着一件带有毛领的灯芯绒夹克。

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:51.460
<v Ira Glass>Sandy Hook deniers saw that in the coverage, and they pounced. "Did he die twice?" "Did he die at all?" So the guy at the bar with Lenny is rattling through all this Pakistan stuff. And then, as Lenny explained to one of my co-workers, Miki Meek, the guy mentions the kid's name-- Noah Pozner.
<v Ira Glass>桑迪胡克阴谋论者在报道中看到了这一点，便立即抓住了它。“他死了两次吗？”“他真的死了吗？”所以，酒吧里那个跟Lenny搭话的人正滔滔不绝地讲述着巴基斯坦的那一堆东西。然后，正如Lenny向我的同事Miki Meek解释的那样，那个人提到了那个孩子的名字——Noah Pozner。

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:56.270
<v Lenny Pozner>I didn't really need to hear much more than that. I just needed to shut him down, basically.
<v Lenny Pozner>我真的不需要再听更多了。我基本上只需要让他闭嘴。

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:57.410
<v Miki Meek>So what did you do?
<v Miki Meek>那你做了什么？

00:01:57.410 --> 00:02:02.460
<v Lenny Pozner>I took out my driver's license, and I said, "Look who you're talking to. You know, show some respect."
<v Lenny Pozner>我拿出我的驾驶执照说：“看看你在跟谁说话。你知道，放尊重点。”

00:02:02.460 --> 00:02:06.900
<v Ira Glass>The boy in the photo was Lenny's son, Noah, who was six when he died.
<v Ira Glass>照片里的男孩是Lenny的儿子Noah，他去世时才六岁。

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.290
<v Miki Meek>Does he connect it, or--
<v Miki Meek>他把这两件事联系起来了，还是——

00:02:08.290 --> 00:02:27.270
<v Lenny Pozner>Oh, sure. He connected it instantly, yeah. And he just became more agitated. Very angered. Went outside and maybe had a cigarette, came back, yelled at me some more. "Oh my god. How much did they pay you? How can you do this?" He was committed to his belief. I was the villain.
<v Lenny Pozner>哦，当然。他立刻就联系起来了，是的。他变得更加激动。非常愤怒。走到外面抽了根烟，回来后又对我大吼大叫。“天哪。他们给了你多少钱？你怎么能这么做？”他坚信自己的想法。我成了反派。

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:59.310
<v Ira Glass>People like this man at the bar pretty much redefined everything about the way Lenny lives his life. Where he lives, how he lives. He runs into these hoaxers in person, and pretty much every day online. They think the government has paid him millions to play the part of a grieving dad. In their minds, Lenny is the sick one. Noah wasn't ever even his kid. And the person who has popularized these theories more than anybody is Alex Jones, who runs the website Infowars, and who pushed these theories with his radio show, and his YouTube videos.
<v Ira Glass>像酒吧里那个男人这样的人，几乎重塑了Lenny生活的方方面面。他住哪里，他如何生活。他在线下会遇到这些骗子，在网上也几乎每天都会遇到。他们认为政府付了他数百万美元，让他扮演一个悲伤的父亲的角色。在他们看来，Lenny才是那个有病的人。Noah甚至根本不是他的孩子。而将这些理论传播得比任何人都广的人是Alex Jones，他经营着InfoWars网站，并通过他的电台节目和YouTube视频推销这些理论。

00:02:59.310 --> 00:03:11.580
<v Ira Glass>Alex Jones made his name right after 9/11, promoting the idea that 9/11 was an attack orchestrated by our own government. With Sandy Hook, Jones said many times that he did not believe the shooting was real.
<v Ira Glass>Alex Jones在“9·11”事件后成名，宣扬“9·11”是由我们自己的政府策划的袭击这一观点。关于桑迪胡克事件，Jones多次表示他不相信枪击案是真的。

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:30.570
<v Alex Jones>Sandy Hook is a synthetic, completely fake, with actors, in my view, manufactured. I couldn't believe it at first. I knew they had actors there, clearly. But I thought they killed some real kids. And it just shows how bold they are, that they clearly used actors.
<v Alex Jones>在我看来，桑迪胡克事件是一个综合性的、彻头彻尾的骗局，有演员参与，是被人为制造出来的。起初我不敢相信。我知道他们肯定用了演员。但我以为他们杀害了一些真正的孩子。这正说明了他们有多大胆，因为他们明显用了演员。

00:03:30.570 --> 00:03:46.920
<v Ira Glass>He's claimed that the government, or some shadowy global forces, are the ones who hired these actors. He and the other hoaxers call them "crisis actors." It's like this whole alternate world that exists right next to the real one. It makes life miserable for parents like Lenny.
<v Ira Glass>他声称政府或某些阴暗的全球势力是聘请这些演员的人。他和那些骗子称他们为“危机演员”。这就像是一个就在现实世界旁边存在的另一个世界。这让像Lenny这样的父母生活变得苦不堪言。

00:03:46.920 --> 00:04:12.870
<v Ira Glass>But unlike most parents in that situation, Lenny decided to go all action hero on the hoaxers, and on Alex Jones. Action hero, I will do what needs to get done to defend my family, damn the consequences. Lenny is resourceful. He is dogged. He does not give up. In this world that we live in of hoaxers and trolls, he has marked out a path that I think few of us would ever want to take. But it is kind of amazing to hear what it entails.
<v Ira Glass>但与大多数处于这种情况的父母不同，Lenny决定像动作英雄一样对待那些骗子和Alex Jones。动作英雄，就是为了捍卫家人，不惜一切后果去做必要的事。Lenny足智多谋。他很执着。他从不放弃。在我们这个充满骗子和喷子的世界里，他走出了一条我想我们极少数人会愿意选择的道路。但听到这其中所包含的内容是相当惊人的。

00:04:12.870 --> 00:04:36.650
<v Ira Glass>Today on our show, we have Lenny's story. And then we have a story from writer Jon Ronson, where he also tries to untangle where this alternate hoaxer world ends and the real one begins. From WBEZ Chicago, it's This American Life. I'm Ira Glass. Stay with us.
<v Ira Glass>今天在我们的节目中，我们将讲述Lenny的故事。然后我们还会有一篇来自作家Jon Ronson的故事，他也试图理清这个虚假的骗子世界在哪里结束，现实世界在哪里开始。来自芝加哥WBEZ电台，这是《美国生活》。我是Ira Glass。请继续收听。

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:53.370
<v Ira Glass>Act One, Down the Rabbit Hole. So our story about the transformation of Lenny Pozner was put together by Miki Meek. I should say there's some curse words in today's program that we have unbeeped for this podcast version of the show. If you prefer a beeped version, it is at our website. Here's Miki.
<v Ira Glass>第一幕，掉进兔子洞。关于Lenny Pozner转变的故事是由Miki Meek制作的。我应该说明一下，今天的节目中有一些脏话，我们在播客版本中没有消音。如果您更喜欢消音版，可以在我们的网站上找到。下面是Miki。

00:04:53.370 --> 00:05:16.420
<v Miki Meek>The first time Lenny became aware of any conspiracy theories about Sandy Hook was about a month after the shooting. He'd been on a media blackout, trying to get through Noah's funeral and taking care of his two young girls. They were also at the elementary school that morning. And one of them was Noah's twin sister. She hid in a separate classroom. But one day, Lenny finally felt ready to go online, read the news, googled his son's name.
<v Miki Meek>Lenny第一次意识到有关桑迪胡克事件的阴谋论是在枪击案发生大约一个月后。他当时正处于媒体封锁状态，试图度过Noah的葬礼并照顾他的两个小女儿。那天早上她们也在那所小学。其中一个是Noah的双胞胎姐姐。她躲在另一间教室里。但有一天，Lenny终于觉得可以上网读读新闻了，于是搜索了他儿子的名字。

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:20.850
<v Lenny Pozner>Infowars was coming up on search results. The forums.
<v Lenny Pozner>InfoWars出现在搜索结果中。还有那些论坛。

00:05:20.850 --> 00:05:21.720
<v Miki Meek>The forums.
<v Miki Meek>论坛。

00:05:21.720 --> 00:05:24.750
<v Lenny Pozner>Yeah. And it's just completely disgusting.
<v Lenny Pozner>是的。简直恶心透顶。

00:05:24.750 --> 00:05:38.910
<v Miki Meek>In just over 30 days, this whole world had been invented. And one of the central pieces of it involved Lenny's wife. Infowars fans were dissecting this one interview she did on CNN. It was with Anderson Cooper just days after Noah's funeral.
<v Miki Meek>在短短30多天里，整个世界就被编造出来了。其中一个核心部分涉及Lenny的妻子。InfoWars的粉丝们在剖析她接受CNN采访时的那一段。那是她在Noah葬礼几天后接受Anderson Cooper采访时的内容。

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:42.080
<v Anderson Cooper>What do you want people to know about Noah?
<v Anderson Cooper>你想让人们了解关于Noah的什么事？

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:54.800
<v Veronique De La Rosa>He loved running and playing with his siblings, and he loved bubble baths and fireflies. And he loved eating the inside of Oreo cookies. And he played the video Gangnam Style ad nauseum.
<v Veronique De La Rosa>他喜欢和兄弟姐妹们一起奔跑玩耍，喜欢泡泡浴和萤火虫。他喜欢吃奥利奥饼干的夹心。他还不厌其烦地播放《江南Style》。

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:59.840
<v Anderson Cooper>I understand he used to tell his siblings that he managed a taco factory.
<v Anderson Cooper>我听说他以前常告诉他的兄弟姐妹们，他经营着一家炸玉米饼工厂。

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:06.530
<v Veronique De La Rosa>Yes, that he was going to split his time as an adult between managing a taco factory and being an astronaut.
<v Veronique De La Rosa>是的，他说他成年后会把时间分配在经营一家炸玉米饼工厂和当宇航员之间。

00:06:06.530 --> 00:06:19.160
<v Miki Meek>The comments online were gross and flimsy. Why didn't she sound sadder? Why would she put on lipstick if she was really grieving? And wasn't she too old to be the mom of a six-year-old kid? They were convinced that something was up.
<v Miki Meek>网上的评论既粗俗又站不住脚。为什么她听起来不够悲伤？如果她真的在悲伤，为什么还要涂口红？她作为一个六岁孩子的母亲是不是太老了？他们确信其中有猫腻。

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:23.480
<v Anderson Cooper>How are you holding up? I mean--
<v Anderson Cooper>你还好吗？我的意思是——

00:06:23.480 --> 00:06:46.070
<v Veronique De La Rosa>Most of the time, I'm kind of numb. I think every mom out there can relate to the fact of how long it takes to create a baby. Those nine months that you watch every ultrasound, and every heartbeat. And it takes nine months to create a human being, and it takes seconds for an AR-15 to take that away from the surface of this earth.
<v Veronique De La Rosa>大多数时候，我有点麻木。我想每一位母亲都能体会到孕育一个婴儿需要多长时间。那九个月里，你看着每一次超声波，每一次心跳。创造一个人需要九个月，而AR-15只需几秒钟就能把他从地球表面抹去。

00:06:46.070 --> 00:07:04.670
<v Miki Meek>This reference to guns was another aha moment for conspiracy theorists. Some of them started digging into Veronique's life, looked up her maiden name, and then said, hey, look at this. There's a Swiss diplomat who has her exact same name. And even fishier, this diplomat once went to an arms control summit at the United Nations.
<v Miki Meek>这种对枪支的提及是阴谋论者的另一个“啊哈时刻”。他们中的一些人开始挖掘Veronique的生活，查她的娘家姓，然后说，嘿，看这个。有个瑞士外交官跟她同名。更可疑的是，这位外交官曾参加过联合国的军备控制峰会。

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:19.840
<v Miki Meek>So maybe they're the same person. Maybe she's one of those elite globalists trying to make guns look bad, so President Obama can repeal the Second Amendment. Suddenly, every real sentiment Veronique shared about Noah was getting reinterpreted as lines from a sinister script.
<v Miki Meek>所以也许她们是同一个人。也许她是那些试图让枪支看起来很糟糕的精英全球主义者之一，这样奥巴马总统就可以废除第二修正案。突然间，Veronique分享的关于Noah的每一个真实感受都被重新解读为邪恶剧本中的台词。

00:07:19.840 --> 00:07:26.950
<v Veronique De La Rosa>They were here, and they mattered. They all have families. And they mattered.
<v Veronique De La Rosa>他们曾经在这里，他们很重要。他们都有家人。他们很重要。

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:44.530
<v Miki Meek>And the kicker that cinched it for these conspiracy theorists? Anderson Cooper's nose. There's this moment when the tip of his nose disappears because of a digital glitch in the video-- what CNN says was normal interference that happens with a live satellite feed. It's just a couple seconds, but hoaxers wouldn't let it go.
<v Miki Meek>而让这些阴谋论者确信这一点的原因是什么？Anderson Cooper的鼻子。视频中有一个时刻，因为数字故障，他的鼻尖消失了——CNN称这在直播卫星信号中是常有的正常干扰。只有几秒钟，但骗子们不肯放过它。

00:07:44.530 --> 00:08:05.330
<v Lenny Pozner>They said that it's a green screen, or a blue screen, or whatever. So that was a fake interview, and Veronique was a participant of a fake, staged CNN interview. That conspiracy theory was all over YouTube, and it was all over YouTube with Noah's image.
<v Lenny Pozner>他们说那是绿幕，或者蓝幕，或其他什么东西。所以那是一次虚假的采访，Veronique是那个虚假、策划好的CNN采访的参与者。那个阴谋论遍布YouTube，而且带着Noah的照片到处传播。

00:08:05.330 --> 00:08:25.160
<v Miki Meek>I've talked to parents who've lost kids in other mass shootings, and they've all been blindsided by online harassment from conspiracy theorists. The crisis actor claim is so common now these attacks usually start almost immediately after victims are IDed in the media. And parents who go on TV and talk about gun control, like Veronique, they get it the worst.
<v Miki Meek>我采访过在其他大规模枪击事件中失去孩子的父母，他们都曾被阴谋论者的网络骚扰搞得措手不及。危机演员的说法现在太普遍了，这些攻击通常在媒体确定受害者身份后几乎立即开始。而像Veronique那样上电视谈论枪支管制的父母，受到的伤害最深。

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:44.750
<v Miki Meek>Sandy Hook is when this really took off. Families get stuck fending off all this crazy hate by themselves. There just aren't that many resources for them, because law enforcement still hasn't figured out how to deal with most cyber harassment, and the tech companies aren't much help. So most families just try to ignore the conspiracy theorists, and hope they'll eventually go away.
<v Miki Meek>桑迪胡克事件是这一切真正开始的时候。家庭只能独自应付所有这些疯狂的仇恨。他们几乎没有什么资源，因为执法部门还没找到如何处理大多数网络骚扰的方法，而科技公司也帮不上什么忙。所以大多数家庭只是试图无视这些阴谋论者，希望他们最终会消失。

00:08:44.750 --> 00:08:53.120
<v Miki Meek>And that's what Lenny did for a while. His life was a wreck. But after about a year and a half, they were still at it, and he couldn't let it go anymore.
<v Miki Meek>这就是Lenny一段时间以来的做法。他的生活一团糟。但大约一年半后，他们依然故我，他再也无法忍受了。

00:08:53.120 --> 00:09:13.640
<v Lenny Pozner>I realized that grieving requires a calmness, and a silence. And all of this material was a distraction for me, and it was noise. And I needed to handle that noise, so that I could have the silence and calm that I needed.
<v Lenny Pozner>我意识到悲伤需要一种平静，一种沉默。所有这些材料对我来说都是一种干扰，它们是噪音。我需要处理这些噪音，这样我才能拥有我所需要的沉默与平静。

00:09:13.640 --> 00:09:35.700
<v Miki Meek>There's this photo I love of Lenny, with his arm wrapped around Noah. He's got a walrus mustache, and he's kneeling on a trampoline with a soft smile. It's spring, and Noah has all this big, brown hair, fat cheeks. He's snuggling his whole body into Lenny's chest. Lenny's got tons of family photos like these, posted them in an online memorial he made for Noah right after he died.
<v Miki Meek>我非常喜欢一张Lenny的照片，他双臂环抱着Noah。他留着海象胡子，跪在蹦床上，带着温柔的微笑。那是春天，Noah留着一头浓密的棕色头发，有着肥嘟嘟的脸颊。他整个人都蜷缩在Lenny的怀里。Lenny有很多这样的家庭照片，他在Noah去世后为他建立的在线纪念馆里发布了这些照片。

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:54.120
<v Miki Meek>The Sandy Hook deniers downloaded them, and repurposed them into cruel memes. Wrote "fake" across Noah's face, took a picture of his headstone and photoshopped under his name, "is not buried here." Photos of his daughters were circulating, too. He couldn't just leave them out there on the web with the trolls.
<v Miki Meek>桑迪胡克否认者下载了这些照片，并把它们重构成残忍的表情包。在Noah的脸上写上“假”，拿走他墓碑的照片，并在他名字下面用Photoshop加上“没有埋在这里”。他女儿的照片也在流传。他不能就这样把它们留在网上任由喷子们摆布。

00:09:54.120 --> 00:10:12.820
<v Miki Meek>Lenny got consumed with thinking about how to take control of the situation, how to extract Noah and his family from all this. The internet didn't scare him. It was actually his comfort zone. He ran his own IT business. He was not the kind of guy who sat around and complained about how something didn't work. He was the guy who fixed stuff.
<v Miki Meek>Lenny沉迷于思考如何控制局面，如何将Noah和他的家人从这一切中解救出来。互联网并没有吓倒他。事实上，那是他的舒适区。他经营着自己的IT业务。他不是那种坐着抱怨事情为什么行不通的人。他是那个解决问题的人。

00:10:12.820 --> 00:10:28.830
<v Lenny Pozner>So you need to find what the problem is, and then find what your solution is, and then start getting closer to that solution, step by step. Otherwise the problem is overwhelming, and then you just want someone else to fix it for you.
<v Lenny Pozner>所以你需要找出问题所在，然后找到解决方案，然后一步步接近那个解决方案。否则问题会让人不知所措，那你只会想让别人替你解决。

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:29.650
<v Miki Meek>Yeah.
<v Miki Meek>是的。

00:10:29.650 --> 00:10:38.080
<v Lenny Pozner>You have to track down where you can make a difference, and get closer to being less broken.
<v Lenny Pozner>你必须找到你能有所作为的地方，并让自己少受一点伤害。

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:50.850
<v Miki Meek>There was one other thing that made Lenny especially qualified to deal with the conspiracy theorists. He used to enjoy those theories himself. The classic fun ones-- Bigfoot, Loch Ness, Area 51, NASA faking the moon landing.
<v Miki Meek>还有一件事使Lenny特别有资格应付阴谋论者。他自己曾经也很享受这些理论。那些经典的有趣的理论——大脚怪、尼斯湖水怪、51区、NASA伪造登月。

00:10:50.850 --> 00:10:52.890
<v Miki Meek>Like, what's the fun of it?
<v Miki Meek>比如，那有什么乐趣？

00:10:52.890 --> 00:11:09.330
<v Lenny Pozner>It's suspending your disbelief. It's like sitting down and watching a science fiction movie, and then looking at the what if. And it's just fun, especially if there's no price to pay in your life, and there's no cost to that way of thinking, then it's just a game.
<v Lenny Pozner>那是暂停你的怀疑。就像坐下来看一部科幻电影，然后看着“如果……会怎样”。这很有趣，特别是如果你的生活中没有代价，这种思维方式也没有损失，那就只是个游戏。

00:11:09.330 --> 00:11:23.700
<v Miki Meek>Sometimes he even listened to Alex Jones in his car. And in fact, just a month after the shootings, when Lenny first saw those things on Alex Jones's website, he tried to reach out. He found a general Infowars email address, and shot him off this message.
<v Miki Meek>有时他甚至在车里听Alex Jones的节目。事实上，就在枪击案发生一个月后，当Lenny第一次在Alex Jones的网站上看到那些东西时，他试图联系他。他找到了一个通用的InfoWars电子邮件地址，发去了这条信息。

00:11:23.700 --> 00:11:43.430
<v Miki Meek>"Alex, I'm very disappointed to see how many people are directing more anger at families that lost their children in Newtown, accusing us of being actors. Haven't we had our share of pain and suffering? I used to enjoy listening to your shows. Now I feel that your type of show created these hateful people, and they need to be reeled in!" Exclamation point.
<v Miki Meek>“Alex，我非常失望地看到有这么多人将更多的愤怒指向在纽敦失去孩子的家庭，指责我们是演员。我们受的痛苦和折磨还不够吗？我以前很喜欢听你的节目。现在我觉得你的节目类型制造了这些可恨的人，他们需要被管教！”感叹号。

00:11:43.430 --> 00:11:46.670
<v Miki Meek>About an hour later, he heard back from Jones' staff.
<v Miki Meek>大约一小时后，他收到了Jones员工的回复。

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:54.050
<v Lenny Pozner>And they responded with "We have not supported the crisis actor claim. We insist that it's a true event." On and on.
<v Lenny Pozner>他们回复说：“我们不支持危机演员的说法。我们坚持认为这是一个真实的事件。”云云。

00:11:54.050 --> 00:12:05.920
<v Miki Meek>This wasn't true. Jones did spread the crisis actor theory. It was on his website at the time, and he started talking about it a lot. That CNN interview with Veronique, he talked about it all the time.
<v Miki Meek>这不是真的。Jones确实传播了危机演员的理论。当时这就在他的网站上，他开始频繁谈论它。关于Veronique的那次CNN采访，他一直在谈论。

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:30.950
<v Alex Jones>Folks, we've got video of Anderson Cooper with clear blue screen out there. He's not there in the town square. We've got people clearly coming up and laughing and then doing the fake crying. We've clearly got people where it's actors playing different parts of different people. I've looked at it, and undoubtedly there's a cover-up. There's actors. They're manipulating. They've been caught lying. And they were pre-planning before it, and then rolled out with it.
<v Alex Jones>伙计们，我们有Anderson Cooper在外面使用清晰蓝幕的视频。他不在镇广场上。我们有人们明显走上前去大笑，然后假装哭泣。我们有明显的人在扮演不同角色的不同人物。我看过了，毫无疑问有一个掩盖行为。有演员。他们在操纵。他们被抓到撒谎。他们在这之前就在预谋，然后带着它出场了。

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:35.510
<v Miki Meek>What Lenny wanted was a one-on-one conversation with Jones, but it didn't happen.
<v Miki Meek>Lenny想要的是与Jones进行一对一的对话，但这并没有发生。

00:12:35.510 --> 00:12:43.550
<v Lenny Pozner>There were a few emails after that, asking me to prove that I'm really who I am, and leading on to get me on the show.
<v Lenny Pozner>在那之后又有几封邮件，要求我证明我的真实身份，并诱导我上节目。

00:12:43.550 --> 00:12:58.760
<v Miki Meek>Lenny didn't want that. He's very private and very reserved, a behind the scenes kind of guy. He's careful when he talks. Things like "no comment," "that's off the record," or "do I have to talk about my personal life?" That came up all the time during our interview.
<v Miki Meek>Lenny不想那样。他非常注重隐私且非常矜持，是一个幕后型的人。他说话很谨慎。像“无可奉告”、“那是非公开的”、“我必须谈论我的个人生活吗？”这样的话在我们的采访中一直出现。

00:12:58.760 --> 00:13:22.850
<v Miki Meek>One of the ground rules he gave is that I had to run his quotes past him and his lawyer, because he's worried about his own safety, if his words were misconstrued. Also, he's fighting some of the conspiracy theories in court. We agreed to his terms. And in the end, he didn't ask me to edit any of his quotes. But he did request that we remove one personal detail, and we did.
<v Miki Meek>他提出的基本规则之一是我必须将他的引语发给他和他的律师审阅，因为如果他的话被曲解，他担心自己的人身安全。此外，他还在法庭上对抗一些阴谋论。我们同意了他的条款。最后，他没有要求我修改他的任何引语。但他确实要求我们删除一个个人细节，我们照做了。

00:13:22.850 --> 00:13:32.720
<v Miki Meek>Now, a year and a half after he reached out to Alex Jones, he decided to try a new tactic. He'd go directly to Jones his followers and the other Sandy Hook conspiracy theorists.
<v Miki Meek>现在，在他联系Alex Jones一年半后，他决定尝试一种新的策略。他要直接针对Jones的追随者和其他桑迪胡克阴谋论者。

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:37.280
<v Veronique De La Rosa>I think his approach was, "I'm going to make them see the light."
<v Veronique De La Rosa>我想他的策略是，“我要让他们看到真相。”

00:13:37.280 --> 00:13:48.260
<v Miki Meek>This is Veronique. She and Lenny were separated when the shooting happened, but were still very much in each other's lives. They decided to start releasing documents about Noah. Report cards, school photos.
<v Miki Meek>这是Veronique。枪击发生时她和Lenny分居，但仍非常密切地参与彼此的生活。他们决定开始发布关于Noah的文件。成绩单、学校照片。

00:13:48.260 --> 00:14:10.190
<v Veronique De La Rosa>He even disclosed Noah's death certificate, which was a difficult decision that we made, but figured, after a while of providing this hard copy convincing evidence that reason would prevail, and they would say, "oh, OK, yeah, you've made your point. I'm going to come around."
<v Veronique De La Rosa>他甚至公开了Noah的死亡证明，这是我们做出的一个艰难决定，但心想，在提供这些确凿的证据一段时间后，理性会占上风，他们会说，“哦，好的，是的，你说的有道理。我会回心转意。”

00:14:10.190 --> 00:14:32.240
<v Miki Meek>Lenny also decided he'd answer anyone's questions. He wanted to join this notorious Facebook group called "Sandy Hook Hoax." It's where a lot of the deniers were congregating and sharing theories. The cover photo on their page looked like it came straight out of a horror movie. A corpse-like girl with a "keep quiet" finger in front of her mouth. The administrator of the Facebook group immediately let him in.
<v Miki Meek>Lenny还决定回答任何人的问题。他想加入那个臭名昭著的Facebook群组“桑迪胡克骗局”。这是很多否认者聚集并分享理论的地方。他们页面上的封面照片看起来像是直接从恐怖电影里出来的。一个僵尸般的女孩，手指放在嘴前做“保持安静”的手势。Facebook群组的管理员立刻让他进去了。

00:14:32.240 --> 00:14:34.900
<v Miki Meek>Do you identify yourself as like, "I am a father?"
<v Miki Meek>你是否表明自己的身份，比如“我是一个父亲？”

00:14:34.900 --> 00:14:38.210
<v Lenny Pozner>They knew who I was. They knew who I was instantly, yeah.
<v Lenny Pozner>他们知道我是谁。他们立刻就知道了，是的。

00:14:38.210 --> 00:14:44.610
<v Miki Meek>To me, it seems so crazy to even go there. Like, this doesn't exactly sound like a group of people who'd want to listen to you.
<v Miki Meek>对我来说，甚至去那里似乎都很疯狂。比如，这听起来并不像是一群你想对他们说话的人。

00:14:44.610 --> 00:15:02.990
<v Lenny Pozner>People who are conspiracy-minded see these tragedies unfold on the internet or on television. They still feel separate from these events. And I considered that bridging that gap could be an important step.
<v Lenny Pozner>有阴谋心态的人在互联网或电视上看到这些悲剧发生。他们仍然觉得与这些事件无关。我认为弥合这一鸿沟可能是一个重要的步骤。

00:15:02.990 --> 00:15:04.500
<v Miki Meek>I can add a human element to this.
<v Miki Meek>我可以给这件事增加一个人性因素。

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:11.030
<v Lenny Pozner>That's right. That's right. And so here I am. I'm the person. So let let's see what happens.
<v Lenny Pozner>没错。没错。所以我就在这儿。我就是那个人。所以让我们看看会发生什么。

00:15:11.030 --> 00:15:12.860
<v Miki Meek>The questions started pouring in.
<v Miki Meek>问题开始接踵而至。

00:15:12.860 --> 00:15:28.520
<v Lenny Pozner>"Why weren't these children rushed to hospitals?" "Why wasn't anything done?" "Why aren't you suing the EMTs?" Or "why aren't you doing this?" "Why wasn't a rescue helicopter called from Hartford?" And I started to recognize some of the patterns that were there.
<v Lenny Pozner>“为什么这些孩子没有被送往医院？”“为什么什么都没做？”“你为什么不起诉急救人员？”或者“你为什么不这样做？”“为什么没有从哈特福德调来救援直升机？”我开始识别出那里的一些模式。

00:15:28.520 --> 00:15:35.060
<v Miki Meek>There were the people you'd expect in a conspiracy group-- anti-gun control people, anti-government people, but also parents.
<v Miki Meek>那里有你在阴谋论组织中会预料到的人——反枪支管制的人、反政府的人，但也有父母。

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:55.900
<v Lenny Pozner>They were young parents with small children, and they just couldn't wrap their minds around the reality that an adult can look at children in their eyes, and pump bullets into their head. They just can't deal with that.
<v Lenny Pozner>他们是带着小孩的年轻父母，他们无法理解这样一个现实：一个成年人可以看着孩子的眼睛，把子弹射进他们的头里。他们只是无法接受这一点。

00:15:55.900 --> 00:16:21.450
<v Miki Meek>The conversation on this Facebook group quickly got ugly and abusive. Some of the members started using anti-Semitic slurs. Lenny was trying everything to keep up a rapport with them, even told them "I listen to Alex Jones in my car. I used to argue with people about 9/11 being an inside job. I entertained that we didn't go to the moon." But it didn't work. So he started blocking people and fighting back. This got him booted from the group.
<v Miki Meek>这个Facebook群组上的对话很快变得丑陋且具有攻击性。一些成员开始使用反犹太主义的诋毁词。Lenny尝试了一切来保持与他们的融洽关系，甚至告诉他们“我在车里听Alex Jones的节目。我以前常和别人争论‘9·11’是内部工作。我还怀疑过我们没有登月。”但这没用。所以他开始屏蔽并回击。这导致他被踢出了群组。

00:16:21.450 --> 00:16:38.030
<v Miki Meek>What's remarkable is just how up for this whole fight he was. When a bunch of people kept private messaging him, Lenny thought, "you know what? I'll just start my own Facebook group." He called it "Conspiracy Theorists Anonymous." This name was meant as a joke. He has a dry sense of humor.
<v Miki Meek>引人注目的是他应对整场战斗的劲头。当一群人不断给他发私人信息时，Lenny想，“你知道吗？我不如自己建一个Facebook群组。”他把它命名为“阴谋论者匿名会”。这个名字是开个玩笑。他有一种冷幽默感。

00:16:38.030 --> 00:17:01.730
<v Miki Meek>Anyway, he made some progress with people, the people who weren't full blown deniers, who actually wanted help parsing out the truth of what really happened. But they dropped away once they got answers. And pretty soon, the only ones left were just dark, sadistic trolls coming in to entertain themselves.
<v Miki Meek>不管怎样，他在人们身上取得了一些进展，那些不是彻头彻尾的否认者，确实想寻求帮助来解析到底发生了什么的人。但当他们得到答案后就离开了。很快，剩下的只有黑暗、虐待狂般的喷子，他们进来是为了取乐。

00:17:01.730 --> 00:17:21.520
<v Miki Meek>One of Lenny's worst trolls was a guy named Wolfgang Halbig. That's his real name, by the way. He's a retired school security expert in Florida, who's probably the number one Newtown hoaxer in the world. This guy traveled to Newtown, appeared as an expert on Alex Jones's show. He's even called for Newtown parents to exhume the bodies of their children to prove that they're dead.
<v Miki Meek>Lenny最糟糕的喷子之一是一个叫Wolfgang Halbig的人。顺便说一句，这是他的真名。他是一位佛罗里达州退休的学校安全专家，可能是世界上头号纽敦骗局制造者。这家伙去过纽敦，作为专家出现在Alex Jones的节目中。他甚至呼吁纽敦的父母开棺验尸，以证明他们的孩子已经死了。

00:17:21.520 --> 00:17:37.960
<v Miki Meek>Halbig ordered a background check on Lenny, then sent it out in an email to lots of people. It was almost 100 pages, listing everything from his social security number and phone number to almost every address he'd ever lived at with photos. Names of his relatives were included too.
<v Miki Meek>Halbig下令对Lenny进行背景调查，然后通过电子邮件发送给很多人。那份调查报告有近100页，列出了他从社会保险号和电话号码到他曾经住过的几乎每个地址及照片的一切信息。他亲戚的名字也包含在内。

00:17:37.960 --> 00:17:52.090
<v Miki Meek>The online harassment had become so intense that Lenny and Veronique, and their two girls, went into hiding. They moved into separate high security gated communities. But Lenny's address kept getting exposed, and hoaxers started posting videos of where he lived.
<v Miki Meek>网络骚扰变得如此强烈，以至于Lenny和Veronique以及他们的两个女儿被迫隐姓埋名。他们搬进了独立的高安全性封闭社区。但Lenny的地址不断被曝光，骗子们开始发布他住处的视频。

00:17:52.090 --> 00:18:24.120
<v Lenny Pozner>One apartment that I had moved into-- I had only lived there, I think, for a month-- and I got a call from a particular hoaxer who happens to be in prison now for attempted murder. And he called me up and was acting like a smart ass, and then read me my social security number, and then read me my address, where I had just moved into. And I said, well, you know what? I don't like this apartment that much, anyway. And I moved shortly after that.
<v Lenny Pozner>有一套我搬进去的公寓——我想我才住了一个月——我就接到了一个骗子的电话，那家伙现在因为谋杀未遂在监狱里。他打电话给我，表现得像个自作聪明的人，然后念出了我的社会保险号，然后念出了我刚搬进去的地址。我说，好吧，你知道吗？我本来就不太喜欢这套公寓。然后不久我就搬走了。

00:18:24.120 --> 00:18:52.710
<v Miki Meek>To try and throw the hoaxers off, Lenny started putting utility bills in different names and got multiple PO boxes all over the place. All this forced Lenny into a new battle strategy. If they were going to expose him, he'd do the same to them. He wrote newspaper op-eds calling out Halbig and the others by name. And when these hoaxers posted his new addresses online, he did the same to them. He also made it so that if you googled their names, the first thing anyone would see was all the Sandy Hook garbage they'd created.
<v Miki Meek>为了试图迷惑这些骗子，Lenny开始用不同的名字缴纳水电费，并到处设立了多个邮政信箱。这一切迫使Lenny采取了一种新的战斗策略。如果他们要曝光他，他也会以其人之道还治其人之身。他写报纸专栏点名Halbig和其他人。当这些骗子在网上发布他的新地址时，他也对他们做了同样的事。他还做到了这一点：如果你搜索他们的名字，任何人看到的第一件事就是他们制造的所有关于桑迪胡克的垃圾。

00:18:52.710 --> 00:19:24.880
<v Miki Meek>And Lenny being Lenny, decided to write a biography about Wolfgang Halbig's life called "The Hoax of a Lifetime." He released it as an e-book. Lenny became the one who knocks. He calls this troll wrestling. It's like trolling the trolls. He gets both energized and sheepish when talking about it. He insists, sometimes the only way to fight hardcore hoaxers is to turn the tables on them. And it worked on some of them, freaked them out.
<v Miki Meek>而身为Lenny的Lenny，决定写一本关于Wolfgang Halbig生平的传记，书名叫《终身的骗局》。他将其作为电子书发布。Lenny成了那个“敲门的人”。他称这为“喷子摔跤”。这就像是在用喷子对付喷子。谈到这一点时，他既充满活力又有点羞怯。他坚持认为，有时对抗铁杆骗子的唯一方法就是以牙还牙。这对他们中的一些人奏效了，吓坏了他们。

00:19:24.880 --> 00:19:40.150
<v Miki Meek>Still, Lenny was just one guy. And every day, new mountains of content about Noah were showing up online. His crusade was a lonely one. The hoaxers seemed so dangerous, most of the other Newtown parents wanted to stay as far away as possible from them.
<v Miki Meek>尽管如此，Lenny只是一个人。每天，网上都会出现关于Noah的新内容。他的远征是孤独的。这些骗子看起来太危险了，大多数其他纽敦父母都想尽可能远离他们。

00:19:40.150 --> 00:20:06.820
<v Lenny Pozner>In my darker moments, the conspiracy part of me would return and ask myself, am I the only one that lost a child? Why am I the only one fighting back? I mean, what the hell is going on? I mean, people were trampling all over other people's children's memories, and those children no longer had a voice to defend themselves. And people were just silent about it.
<v Lenny Pozner>在我比较黑暗的时刻，我内心阴谋论的那一部分会回来问自己，我是唯一失去孩子的人吗？为什么我是唯一一个反击的人？我的意思是，这到底是怎么回事？我的意思是，人们在践踏其他人的孩子的记忆，而那些孩子不再有声音来为自己辩护。而人们对此保持沉默。

00:20:06.820 --> 00:20:31.170
<v Miki Meek>But while Lenny was escalating his tactics, so was the other side. Around the second anniversary of Sandy Hook, a small group of conspiracy theorists made an almost three hour movie on YouTube, questioning the shooting. They described themselves as independent journalists and researchers, but their backgrounds were totally random. They included a magician, the owner of a moving company, a guy who'd been arrested for stabbing someone five times, and a stay-at-home dad.
<v Miki Meek>但当Lenny升级他的策略时，对方也在升级。在桑迪胡克两周年纪念日左右，一小群阴谋论者在YouTube上制作了一部近三小时的电影，质疑这次枪击事件。他们自称为独立记者和研究人员，但他们的背景完全是随机的。其中包括一名魔术师、一家搬家公司的老板、一个曾因捅人五刀而被捕的家伙，以及一名全职爸爸。

00:20:31.170 --> 00:20:35.530
<v Doug Maguire>I just had an idea that I wanted to be an underground filmmaker myself.
<v Doug Maguire>我只是有个想法，我想自己成为一名地下电影制片人。

00:20:35.530 --> 00:21:03.760
<v Miki Meek>This is Doug Maguire. He says he met this group online, on YouTube, and got brought in at the end to help polish the movie. It felt exciting. At the time, Doug was a struggling filmmaker in Los Angeles. Occasionally did some stunt work. He got into conspiracy theories the way lots of people do-- watching them on YouTube. Like Lenny, he loved the ones about Bigfoot and UFOs. But then he went to look up news about Sandy Hook, and YouTube's recommendation system started suggesting hoax videos.
<v Miki Meek>这是Doug Maguire。他说他在网上、在YouTube上遇到了这个组织，并被拉进去帮助润色这部电影。这感觉很令人兴奋。当时，Doug在洛杉矶是一名苦苦挣扎的电影制片人。偶尔做一些特技工作。他像许多人一样迷上了阴谋论——通过YouTube观看它们。像Lenny一样，他喜欢关于大脚怪和不明飞行物的理论。但后来他去查询关于桑迪胡克的新闻，YouTube的推荐系统开始向他推荐骗局视频。

00:21:03.760 --> 00:21:12.940
<v Miki Meek>He didn't believe the theory that the kids were actors. He thought children died, but he felt pretty sure there was some other kind of cover up going on, maybe one with the mafia.
<v Miki Meek>他不相信孩子们是演员的说法。他认为孩子们确实死了，但他觉得肯定还有其他某种掩盖行动，也许是和黑手党有关的。

00:21:12.940 --> 00:21:18.250
<v Miki Meek>And where did you get that information? Like, where did you come up with this idea of a mob? Had you read this somewhere?
<v Miki Meek>你是从哪里得到这些信息的？比如，你是怎么想出黑帮这个主意的？你是在哪里读到的吗？

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:24.270
<v Doug Maguire>No, it was-- you know, because I make movies. So I think I have an active imagination.
<v Doug Maguire>不，那是——你知道，因为我制作电影。所以我认为我有活跃的想象力。

00:21:24.270 --> 00:21:26.530
<v Miki Meek>I'm confused. What was your thinking?
<v Miki Meek>我糊涂了。你的想法是什么？

00:21:26.530 --> 00:21:34.710
<v Doug Maguire>A family had done someone wrong. Like, let's say the movie Goodfellas, OK? Henry Hill is hiding out in a little village.
<v Doug Maguire>一个家庭对某人做了坏事。比如，就说《好家伙》这部电影吧，好吗？Henry Hill躲在一个小村庄里。

00:21:34.710 --> 00:21:58.060
<v Miki Meek>He also mentioned Kindergarten Cop. When they released their film, they uploaded it to a bunch of different accounts, on places like YouTube, Vimeo, Dailymotion. Pretty soon, it was showing up everywhere. To combat this, Lenny had to change tactics one final time. No more talking to hoaxers one-on-one. Now the thing he'd focus on was content removal, scrubbing their stuff off the internet.
<v Miki Meek>他还提到了《幼儿园警探》。当他们发行电影时，他们将其上传到许多不同的账户上，在YouTube、Vimeo、Dailymotion等地。很快，它到处都在出现。为了对抗这一点，Lenny不得不最后一次改变策略。不再与骗子一对一地交谈。现在他要关注的是内容删除，把他们的东西从互联网上清除掉。

00:21:58.060 --> 00:22:15.460
<v Miki Meek>He decided he was going to get every single copy of the movie taken down, which wasn't going to be easy. He couldn't just write into YouTube and say, "hey, this video is full of lies." That wasn't going to be enough. The internet is full of lies. He needed something else. And he realized he had it.
<v Miki Meek>他决定要把电影的每一份拷贝都下架，这并不容易。他不能只是给YouTube写信说，“嘿，这个视频全是谎言。”那是不够的。互联网上到处都是谎言。他需要别的东西。而他意识到他有。

00:22:15.460 --> 00:22:44.080
<v Miki Meek>These conspiracy theorists had used photos and videos of him and Noah and Veronique. Those were his property, making this movie a copyright violation. The stolen images were now a useful weapon. Lenny tracked down every place where this video was posted. And you've probably seen this. There's a little button you can click on to report stuff. So that's what he did for hours every day. And success. Sort of. The hoaxers kept reposting and moving the video onto other sites.
<v Miki Meek>这些阴谋论者使用了他和Noah还有Veronique的照片和视频。那是他的财产，这使得这部电影构成版权侵权。被窃取的图像现在是一个有用的武器。Lenny追踪了发布这个视频的每一个地方。你可能见过这个。有一个小按钮可以点击来举报东西。所以这就是他每天花几小时做的事情。成功了。某种程度上。骗子们不断转发并将视频移动到其他网站上。

00:22:44.080 --> 00:22:57.520
<v Lenny Pozner>You know, the crazies are not running the asylum. It's the platforms who are allowing this to go on. So that solidifies it for me that we have to just remove all of this garbage, and that's all we need to do.
<v Lenny Pozner>你知道，疯子们并没有在经营精神病院。是那些允许这一切发生的平台。所以这对我来说更坚定了这一点：我们必须删除所有这些垃圾，而这就是我们需要做的全部。

00:22:57.520 --> 00:23:00.850
<v Miki Meek>But this, of course, pissed off a lot of hoaxers.
<v Miki Meek>但这当然激怒了许多骗子。

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:04.720
<v Alex Jones>We don't know what's going on. We just know it doesn't look right.
<v Alex Jones>我们不知道发生了什么。我们只知道它看起来不对劲。

00:23:04.720 --> 00:23:12.970
<v Miki Meek>Alex Jones. He was stumped. Lenny had successfully forced the Infowars site to remove pictures of Noah using copyright.
<v Miki Meek>Alex Jones。他被难住了。Lenny已成功利用版权迫使InfoWars网站删除了Noah的照片。

00:23:12.970 --> 00:23:35.720
<v Alex Jones>So frustrating. This is amazing. The claimant is Lenny Pozner. They think because they can hold out some little kids and say, we're shutting peoples' websites down because they're belittling the memory of these children. No, we're not. But even if we were, you couldn't violate our first amendment, because that's what it's there for. And if you take our rights, you take everybody's rights.
<v Alex Jones>太令人沮丧了。这太惊人了。原告是Lenny Pozner。他们认为因为他们可以举着一些小孩子，说我们要关闭人们的网站，因为他们在贬低这些孩子的记忆。不，我们没有。但即使我们有，你也不能违反我们的第一修正案，因为这就是它存在的原因。如果你剥夺了我们的权利，你就剥夺了所有人的权利。

00:23:35.720 --> 00:23:41.750
<v Miki Meek>And Jones put one of the guys who worked on the movie on the air. His name is Brian. He's from Alabama.
<v Miki Meek>Jones把参与制作电影的一个家伙带上了节目。他叫Brian。他来自阿拉巴马州。

00:23:41.750 --> 00:23:46.990
<v Alex Jones>What do you think of us being censored? What's been happening to you?
<v Alex Jones>你对我们被审查有什么看法？你经历了什么？

00:23:46.990 --> 00:23:55.480
<v Brian>I can tell you lots about Lenny. This man is something that you've never seen before. He's got a group of trolls.
<v Brian>我可以告诉你很多关于Lenny的事情。这个人是你从未见过的。他有一群喷子。

00:23:55.480 --> 00:24:08.030
<v Alex Jones>I mean, they're trying to shut us down, when we're just investigating it and looking at all sides, it must be horrible for folks out there that vehemently think this is staged. So just specifically, what have you gone through?
<v Alex Jones>我的意思是，当我们只是在调查它并从各个角度看待它时，他们却试图关闭我们，这对那些坚决认为这是演戏的人来说一定很糟糕。所以具体来说，你经历了什么？

00:24:08.030 --> 00:24:25.370
<v Brian>I can't even put up a video showing that he has put up a copyright strike against me without him copywriting striking that. These people are vile. And Lenny, if you're listening, your day is coming, my friend. It is coming.
<v Brian>我甚至不能发布一个视频来展示他对我有版权打击，而他不对此进行版权打击。这些人很卑鄙。Lenny，如果你在听，你的日子到了，我的朋友。它到了。

00:24:25.370 --> 00:24:30.860
<v Alex Jones>Wow. I mean, this sounds like a war is going on. I think they made a major mistake involving us.
<v Alex Jones>哇。我的意思是，这听起来像是一场战争正在进行。我认为他们招惹我们犯了大错。

00:24:30.860 --> 00:24:36.330
<v Brian>Oh, I totally agree. They don't know what they bit off. Go after him, Alex. Crush him.
<v Brian>哦，我完全同意。他们不知道他们咬了什么。去对付他，Alex。粉碎他。

00:24:36.330 --> 00:25:03.800
<v Miki Meek>In this video on YouTube, Jones showed his fans-- he had millions of them-- Lenny's email, the city he lived in, and the address he picked up his mail. Even held up some satellite shots from Google Earth. Lenny got this video taken down too, flagging it for privacy violations. But it didn't matter. The hoaxers had taken on a mob mentality, pursuing and harassing Lenny. This is an Infowars fan named Lucy Richards, who left multiple death threats on Lenny's phone.
<v Miki Meek>在这个YouTube视频中，Jones向他的粉丝——他有数百万粉丝——展示了Lenny的电子邮件、他居住的城市以及他取件的地址。甚至还举出了一些来自谷歌地球的卫星镜头。Lenny也把这个视频下架了，因为隐私违规标记了它。但这没用。骗子们已经形成了一种暴民心态，追求并骚扰Lenny。这是一个叫Lucy Richards的InfoWars粉丝，她在Lenny的电话里留下了多次死亡威胁。

00:25:03.800 --> 00:25:25.370
<v Lucy Richards>Did you hide your imaginary son in an attic? Are you still fucking him, you fucking Jew bastard? You're gonna die. You're gonna rot in hell. Death is coming to you real soon, and there's nothing you can do about it. So you're just gonna have to take it, OK? Jew bastard. Look behind you. Death is coming to you real soon.
<v Lucy Richards>你把你的虚构儿子藏在阁楼里了吗？你还在强奸他吗，你这个操蛋的犹太混蛋？你会死的。你会在地狱里腐烂。死亡很快就会降临到你身上，你什么也做不了。所以你只能承受，好吗？犹太混蛋。看你身后。死亡很快就会降临到你身上。

00:25:25.370 --> 00:25:50.160
<v Miki Meek>She said, "Look behind you. Death is coming to you real soon." Lenny was already living in hiding. He'd moved multiple times by then, because hoaxers kept tracking down his address. But now the chances that a hoaxer might show up at his door and kill him suddenly felt much higher. His kids were living with him half the week, and he worried about them. At the same time, he didn't consider stopping. He didn't think it would make them safer.
<v Miki Meek>她说，“看你身后。死亡很快就会降临到你身上。”Lenny当时已经在躲藏了。在那之前他已经搬了好几次家，因为骗子们不断追踪他的地址。但现在一个骗子可能出现在门口杀他的可能性感觉突然高得多了。他的孩子半周和他住在一起，他很为她们担心。与此同时，他没考虑停止。他不认为这会使她们更安全。

00:25:50.160 --> 00:26:26.130
<v Lenny Pozner>That's one of the misconceptions that exist, that people think that I am only targeted because of challenging the content. And that's not the case. I took the action because I was being targeted. So if my address was published all over the internet, my photo was published all over the internet, and my living children's photos are published online, that's existed before I did anything. I didn't cause the targeting. It was already there. I was minimizing the targeting.
<v Lenny Pozner>这是存在的误解之一，人们认为我受到针对只是因为质疑了内容。事实并非如此。我采取行动是因为我受到了针对。所以如果我的地址被发布在整个互联网上，我的照片被发布在整个互联网上，我活着孩子的照片被发布在网上，那是发生在我做任何事情之前就存在的。我没有造成针对。它已经在那里了。我是在最小化针对。

00:26:26.130 --> 00:26:58.420
<v Miki Meek>He posted receipts for firearms. I'd asked if he actually bought them, and he wouldn't give me an answer. Amidst all this, Lenny kept up his daily ritual. He'd wake up, make coffee, and then sit in front of his computer for hours, flagging content, trying to systematically erase Noah from the Sandy Hook hoax story. There was a lot of stuff he couldn't invoke copyright law for, like the death threats and harassment. That was much harder to get taken down.
<v Miki Meek>他张贴了枪支收据。我问他是否真的买了它们，他没有给我答案。在这一切之中，Lenny继续他每天的仪式。他起床，煮咖啡，然后坐在电脑前几个小时，标记内容，试图系统地将Noah从桑迪胡克骗局的故事中抹去。有很多东西他不能诉诸版权法，比如死亡威胁和骚扰。那些要下架要困难得多。

00:26:58.420 --> 00:27:21.760
<v Miki Meek>The tech companies were wary of becoming arbiters of truth, making decisions about what its users could and couldn't say. But Lenny, in his usual methodical fashion, kept chipping away. On YouTube, he kept a scorecard. Once he nailed someone with three copyright strikes, YouTube would remove their accounts. He killed thousands of videos this way. The hoaxers called this "getting Poznered." He'd become a hashtag.
<v Miki Meek>科技公司对成为真理的仲裁者感到谨慎，对用户可以和不可以说什么做出决定。但Lenny以他一贯条理分明的方式，不断挖掘。在YouTube上，他保留了一张记分卡。一旦他用三次版权打击抓住某人，YouTube就会删除他们的账户。他用这种方式杀死了成千上万个视频。骗子们称这为“被Pozner化”。他成了标签。

00:27:21.760 --> 00:27:37.690
<v Miki Meek>Then he and Veronique helped get a professor in Florida, named James Tracy, fired. This guy had harassed them for years, and kept using Noah's image to promote his conspiracy theories. He's also the one who helped popularize the conspiracy term "crisis actor" on his blog right after the shooting.
<v Miki Meek>然后他和Veronique帮助佛罗里达州一位名叫James Tracy的教授被解雇。这家伙骚扰了他们多年，并一直使用Noah的照片来推销他的阴谋论。他也是枪击案后在他博客上推广阴谋论术语“危机演员”的人。

00:27:37.690 --> 00:28:04.300
<v Miki Meek>And that woman who was leaving death threats, Lucy Richards? Lenny reported her to the police, and they arrested her. She was sentenced to five months in jail. The judge rebuked her for going after Lenny, saying, quote, "This is a reality, and there is no fiction. There are no alternative facts." He barred her from Infowars and other conspiracy websites as one of the conditions of her parole.
<v Miki Meek>还有那个留下死亡威胁的女人Lucy Richards？Lenny向警方举报了她，他们逮捕了她。她被判入狱五个月。法官斥责她针对Lenny，引用道：“这是一个现实，没有虚构。没有替代事实。”他禁止她访问InfoWars和其他阴谋论网站，作为她假释条件之一。

00:28:04.300 --> 00:28:30.840
<v Miki Meek>One surprising thing that happened over the years is that some of the hoaxers who used to harass Lenny flipped to his side. There were dozens of them. Lenny says these were people who came to him only after they changed their own minds, not people he tried to convert. He says that never works. It's a waste of time. Some of them became disenchanted when they saw Sandy Hook hoaxers who were more interested in photo shopping evidence and getting online followers than tracking down the truth.
<v Miki Meek>多年来发生的一件令人惊讶的事情是，一些曾经骚扰Lenny的骗子翻转到了他这一边。有几十个。Lenny说这些人是在改变主意后才来到他身边的，而不是他试图转化的人。他说那从来不起作用。那是浪费时间。他们中的一些人在看到桑迪胡克骗局制造者对Photoshop证据和获取网络追随者的兴趣超过追踪真相时，感到幻灭。

00:28:30.840 --> 00:28:38.780
<v Miki Meek>One of them was Doug, who worked on that hoaxer movie about Sandy Hook. In 2016, he found a phone number for Lenny and left a voicemail.
<v Miki Meek>其中一个是Doug，他参与了那部关于桑迪胡克的骗局电影。2016年，他找到了Lenny的电话号码并留下了语音邮件。

00:28:38.780 --> 00:28:50.730
<v Doug Maguire>"Hey, Lenny Pozner, this is dickhead Doug Maguire. If you ever need me, if you ever want to get a hold of me and learn about what all these people are up to, here's my number."
<v Doug Maguire>“嘿，Lenny Pozner，这是混蛋Doug Maguire。如果你需要我，如果你想联系我并了解这些人都在干什么，这是我的号码。”

00:28:50.730 --> 00:28:53.940
<v Miki Meek>Did you apologize in that message?
<v Miki Meek>你在那条信息里道歉了吗？

00:28:53.940 --> 00:28:55.890
<v Doug Maguire>I don't believe I did.
<v Doug Maguire>我不相信我道歉了。

00:28:55.890 --> 00:29:12.960
<v Miki Meek>Not surprisingly, Lenny didn't return his call. Doug was reaching out to Lenny because the hoaxers had turned on him, too. He says he started feuding with some of them after he made a video exposing a Christian YouTuber who was making money off false, outrageous claims. All of his social media accounts then got hacked.
<v Miki Meek>不出所料，Lenny没有回他的电话。Doug联系Lenny是因为骗子们也转而针对他了。他说，在他制作了一个揭露一名靠虚假、令人发指的说法赚钱的基督教YouTuber的视频后，他开始与他们中的一些人发生争执。他所有的社交媒体账户随后都被黑了。

00:29:12.960 --> 00:29:37.770
<v Miki Meek>Lenny was the only person he could think of who knew how to fight back. He wanted advice. So he tried him again, and got through. He told Lenny that it felt like he'd been sort of brainwashed. That he'd been on a roller coaster ride, that he wanted to switch sides. Lenny had started a nonprofit called The HONR Network, where volunteers help families from mass tragedies fight digital harassment. So Doug began helping him scrub content.
<v Miki Meek>Lenny是他能想到的唯一知道如何反击的人。他想要建议。所以他再次尝试，并成功接通了。他告诉Lenny感觉自己像是被洗脑了。说他一直在坐过山车，他想换边。Lenny创办了一个叫HONR Network的非营利组织，志愿者们帮助大悲剧受害家庭对抗数字骚扰。所以Doug开始帮助他清除内容。

00:29:37.770 --> 00:29:41.350
<v Miki Meek>When you were doing it, did you feel like you were doing penance?
<v Miki Meek>当你在做的时候，你觉得你在赎罪吗？

00:29:41.350 --> 00:29:50.030
<v Doug Maguire>Yeah. Yeah, and my heart is very heavy for this.
<v Doug Maguire>是的。是的，我为此感到沉重。

00:29:50.030 --> 00:29:57.730
<v Miki Meek>Were you surprised at how quickly Lenny let you in?
<v Miki Meek>你对Lenny让你加入的速度感到惊讶吗？

00:29:57.730 --> 00:30:14.780
<v Doug Maguire>Yeah, and I still am. The fact that he even is giving me a chance, I'm very humbled. I tell him I love him. I tell him that he's like my mentor. Sometimes, I call him "boss," and he says, "don't call me boss."
<v Doug Maguire>是的，现在也是。他甚至给我机会这一事实，我感到非常谦卑。我告诉他我爱他。我告诉他他就像我的导师。有时，我叫他“老板”，他说，“别叫我老板。”

00:30:14.780 --> 00:30:17.210
<v Doug Maguire>[CHUCKLING]
<v Doug Maguire>[轻笑]

00:30:17.210 --> 00:30:20.400
<v Miki Meek>Have you you apologized to other families at Sandy Hook?
<v Miki Meek>你向桑迪胡克的其他家庭道歉了吗？

00:30:20.400 --> 00:31:01.000
<v Doug Maguire>No. I think just to try to call up one of these families that-- they don't need to hear from some kind of a YouTuber guy in Los Angeles. I think, one day-- I am very sorry. Very sorry for any problems to any victims.
<v Doug Maguire>没有。我认为试图给这些家庭中的任何一个打电话——他们不需要从洛杉矶的某个YouTuber那里听到什么。我想，有一天——我非常抱歉。对任何受害者造成的任何问题都非常抱歉。

00:31:01.000 --> 00:31:20.200
<v Miki Meek>Doug is now one of Lenny's most devoted volunteers. Lenny's got more than 100 people helping him out at any given time. But the burnout rate is high because the work is so intense. And hoaxers harass volunteers like Doug all the time for helping Lenny.
<v Miki Meek>Doug现在是Lenny最忠诚的志愿者之一。Lenny随时都有100多人帮助他。但倦怠率很高，因为工作太紧张了。而且骗子们一直因为Doug帮助Lenny而骚扰他。

00:31:20.200 --> 00:31:40.480
<v Miki Meek>When Lenny Googles Noah's name now, he no longer gets page after page of hoaxer content. A lot of it is gone now. Instead, the first hits that come up are news articles about Lenny's fight to make the tech companies more accountable. For years, he's been criticizing them in the press for not doing more to protect families of mass tragedies from online abuse.
<v Miki Meek>当Lenny现在谷歌Noah的名字时，他不再得到一页又一页的骗局内容。现在很多都不见了。相反，出现的第一条是关于Lenny为使科技公司承担更多责任而进行斗争的新闻文章。多年来，他一直批评他们在媒体上，因为没有采取更多措施保护大悲剧家庭免受网络暴力。

00:31:40.480 --> 00:31:59.560
<v Miki Meek>Last summer, he and Veronique called out Mark Zuckerberg in an open letter in The Guardian. They wrote, quote "you, arguably the most powerful man on the planet, have deemed that the attacks on us are immaterial, that providing assistance in removing threats is too cumbersome, and that our lives are less important than providing a safe haven for hate."
<v Miki Meek>去年夏天，他和Veronique在《卫报》的一封公开信中点名Mark Zuckerberg。他们写道，引用道：“你，可以说地球上最有权势的人，认为对我们的攻击无关紧要，提供帮助删除威胁太麻烦，我们的生活不如为仇恨提供避风港重要。”

00:31:59.560 --> 00:32:20.420
<v Miki Meek>Shortly after, Facebook reached out to Lenny. He started working with their content moderators and policymakers, and says their response times are now much faster. He also helped turn up the heat on Alex Jones. Last spring, he and Veronique and another dad from Newtown filed defamation lawsuits against him. Other parents followed with their own suit.
<v Miki Meek>不久之后，Facebook联系了Lenny。他开始与他们的内容版主和决策者合作，并表示他们的响应时间现在快多了。他还帮助给Alex Jones施压。去年春天，他和Veronique以及纽敦的另一位父亲对他提起了诽谤诉讼。其他父母也跟着提起了自己的诉讼。

00:32:20.420 --> 00:32:51.320
<v Miki Meek>A few months later, Apple started removing Jones's material from iTunes, saying they would not, quote, tolerate hate speech. Facebook, Google, and Spotify then followed suit. YouTube killed his channel completely, but you can still find his videos on the platform. And Twitter was one of the last to take action against Jones and Infowars. The New York Times reported that getting deplatformed cut his online audience nearly in half.
<v Miki Meek>几个月后，苹果开始从iTunes中删除Jones的材料，称他们不会，引用道，容忍仇恨言论。Facebook、谷歌和Spotify随后效仿。《纽约时报》报道称，被剥夺平台削减了他的网络受众近一半。

00:32:51.320 --> 00:33:10.470
<v Miki Meek>I met up with Lenny at his place recently. He lives in a gated high security residence. He was filing copyright and harassment reports to places like Instagram, Pinterest, Reddit, Vimeo, and Twitter. He says Twitter is his biggest headache right now. There's content about Noah he still can't get down, and he gets personally attacked there all the time.
<v Miki Meek>我最近在Lenny的住处和他见面。他住在一个封闭的高安全住所里。他正在向Instagram、Pinterest、Reddit、Vimeo和Twitter等地方提交版权和骚扰报告。他说Twitter是他现在最大的头痛。关于Noah的内容他仍然无法删除，而且他一直在那里受到个人攻击。

00:33:10.470 --> 00:33:16.670
<v Miki Meek>Do you feel like you've jumped in this rabbit hole that is never going to end?
<v Miki Meek>你觉得你掉进了这个永远不会结束的兔子洞吗？

