<v Jacob Olsen>Who told you that? No. No.
<v Jacob Olsen>谁告诉你的？不。不。

00:44:52.030 --> 00:45:03.560
<v Jon  Ronson>And Lina found the police officer who actually worked in the school when Alex was there, who presumably would have been one of the drug dealing cops who beat up Alex. His name is Terry Garrett.
<v Jon  Ronson>Lina找到了在Alex在那里时确实在学校工作的警察，大概他会是打Alex的贩毒警察之一。他的名字是Terry Garrett。

00:45:03.560 --> 00:45:05.960
<v Jon  Ronson>[LAUGHTER]
<v Jon  Ronson>[笑声]

00:45:05.960 --> 00:45:23.790
<v Terry Garrett>OK, that sounds like something he probably would say, but I don't think anything like that ever happened. I mean, I would be willing to bet my whole pension that that never happened. I mean, I don't think there were any times where, actually, we were even questioning a student, that an administrator wasn't in the room.
<v Terry Garrett>好的，那听起来像是他可能会说的话，但我认为从来没有发生过那种事。我的意思是，我愿意拿我整个养老金打赌那从来没有发生过。我的意思是，我不认为有任何时候，事实上，我们在审问学生时，办公室里没有管理员在场。

00:45:23.790 --> 00:45:56.240
<v Jon  Ronson>What everyone does remember about Alex is, well, how memorable he was. We were emailed the same stories over and over from former classmates. Quote, "he used to run through the hall saying he was the devil. This is no joke." And, "he spoke a lot about being Satan or the Antichrist." And, "he would walk the halls with his arms flared out, with this intense, wide-eyed, evil look in his eyes." And, "he proclaimed to be the Antichrist."
<v Jon  Ronson>每个人都记得关于Alex的是，嗯，他是多么令人难忘。我们一遍又一遍地收到前同学发来的同样的故事。引用道，“他过去常跑过大厅说他是魔鬼。这不是开玩笑。”还有，“他说了很多关于成为撒旦或反基督的事情。”还有，“他会走过大厅，手臂张开，带着那种强烈、睁大眼睛、邪恶的眼神。”还有，“他宣称自己是反基督。”

00:45:56.240 --> 00:45:58.060
<v Jon  Ronson>Here's Coach Randy.
<v Jon  Ronson>这是Randy教练。

00:45:58.060 --> 00:46:10.990
<v Randall Talley>I'm fixing to tell you something that's gonna blow your mind. He-- oh, golly. People thought he was possessed. Have you heard this?
<v Randall Talley>我要告诉你一些会让你大吃一惊的事。他——哦，天哪。人们认为他被附身了。你听过这个吗？

00:46:10.990 --> 00:46:15.520
<v Lina Misitzis>I've heard this from so many students, but this is the first time I've heard it from an adult.
<v Lina Misitzis>我从很多学生那里听到过这个，但这还是我第一次从成年人那里听到。

00:46:15.520 --> 00:46:32.800
<v Randall Talley>Well, he could make his tongue turn black. And he would roll his eyes back in his head, and he would just sort of shake his head. It was-- I don't even know how to describe it, it was so eerie.
<v Randall Talley>嗯，他能让他的舌头变黑。他会把眼睛翻到头里去，他会只是那种摇摇头。那是——我甚至不知道怎么描述它，它太令人毛骨悚然了。

00:46:32.800 --> 00:46:34.750
<v Lina Misitzis>So you would see him do it?
<v Lina Misitzis>所以你会看到他这样做？

00:46:34.750 --> 00:46:37.060
<v Randall Talley>Yeah, I saw him do it in class.
<v Randall Talley>是的，我在课堂上看到他这样做。

00:46:37.060 --> 00:46:39.580
<v Lina Misitzis>And what did you think you were looking at?
<v Lina Misitzis>你认为你在看什么？

00:46:39.580 --> 00:46:46.390
<v Randall Talley>I really didn't know if he had broke a pen, or something, you know, to get his tongue, and his mouth black, or not.
<v Randall Talley>我真的不知道他是否弄坏了一支笔，或其他什么，你知道，去弄黑他的舌头和嘴。

00:46:46.390 --> 00:46:54.310
<v Ellen>He terrorized that high school. Just run full steam, and shove his head into the lockers, and scream, "Hail Satan."
<v Ellen>他恐吓了那所高中。只是全速奔跑，把头塞进储物柜，尖叫，“撒旦万岁。”

00:46:54.310 --> 00:47:19.020
<v Jon  Ronson>This is Ellen. I'll call her "Ellen." She didn't want us to use her real name because, as she texted, "I am not afraid of Alex directly, but I am very concerned about retaliation from his followers." Ellen went to middle school and high school with Alex. She didn't remember any party in a barn where Alex got revenge attacked, but she did have lots other memories of him, like these.
<v Jon  Ronson>这是Ellen。我会叫她“Ellen”。她不想让我们用她的真名，因为，正如她发短信说，“我不直接害怕Alex，但我非常担心他追随者的报复。”Ellen和Alex一起上初中和高中。她不记得Alex被复仇攻击的谷仓里的任何派对，但她确实有很多其他关于他的记忆，比如这些。

00:47:19.020 --> 00:47:34.920
<v Ellen>Sitting in art class with him, across the table-- he's over there wringing his hands, describing to me in great detail how he's going to rape me. And I never thought he would actually do that. Just shock factor.
<v Ellen>和他一起坐在艺术课上，在桌子对面——他在那里绞着手，向我详细描述他打算如何强奸我。我从来没想过他真的会那样做。只是为了冲击力。

00:47:34.920 --> 00:47:40.170
<v Jon Ronson>If Alex hadn't become famous, would you still have remembered Alex?
<v Jon Ronson>如果Alex没出名，你还会记得Alex吗？

00:47:40.170 --> 00:47:44.240
<v Ellen>Oh, yes. Definitely. You don't forget people like that.
<v Ellen>哦，是的。当然。你不会忘记那样的人。

00:47:44.240 --> 00:47:48.000
<v Jon  Ronson>Then Ellen told me her worst Alex memory.
<v Jon  Ronson>然后Ellen告诉了我她最坏的Alex记忆。

00:47:48.000 --> 00:48:08.210
<v Ellen>The most violent incident was-- in second period geography? Where he bludgeoned one of his closest friends to the point where he was unconscious, and bleeding, and laying on the floor.
<v Ellen>最暴力的事件是——在第二节地理课上？他打他最亲密的朋友之一，打到他失去知觉，流血，躺在地板上。

00:48:08.210 --> 00:48:10.510
<v Jon Ronson>Was that Jared?
<v Jon Ronson>那是Jared吗？

00:48:10.510 --> 00:48:12.370
<v Ellen>Mm-hm.
<v Ellen>嗯嗯。

00:48:12.370 --> 00:48:15.580
<v Jon Ronson>So when did you first meet Alex Jones?
<v Jon Ronson>那么你第一次见到Alex Jones是什么时候？

00:48:15.580 --> 00:48:18.600
<v Jared>1990. My senior year.
<v Jared>1990年。我高三那年。

00:48:18.600 --> 00:48:34.680
<v Jon  Ronson>Jared's real name is Jared. He still lives close to Rockwall, in a mobile home in the countryside. Even though his mother, who is watching us from the kitchen, had counseled him to be anonymous, Jared was steadfast. He wanted to be named.
<v Jon  Ronson>Jared的真名是Jared。他仍然住在Rockwall附近，在乡村的一辆移动房屋里。尽管他母亲，在厨房里看着我们，建议他匿名，但Jared很坚定。他想被命名。

00:48:34.680 --> 00:48:49.060
<v Jared>Right off the bat, he was odd. Real odd, real strange. We wanted him around because it was funny at first, you know? The way he acted. But it got worse and worse, and finally, man, we just didn't want to hang out with him at all.
<v Jared>一开始，他就很奇怪。真奇怪，真陌生。我们想让他待在周围，因为起初很有趣，你知道吗？他的行为方式。但它变得越来越糟，最后，伙计，我们只是根本不想和他在一起了。

00:48:49.060 --> 00:49:00.170
<v Jon  Ronson>Jared was bewildered that a journalist had contacted him. Nobody had asked him about the day Alex beat him unconscious since high school. It was an argument over a girl.
<v Jon  Ronson>Jared对记者联系他感到困惑。自高中以来，没有人问过他Alex打他到失去知觉那天的事。这是一个关于女孩的争论。

00:49:00.170 --> 00:49:32.830
<v Jared>I said, what's going on? But he came in behind me, and pretty much just rammed into the wall, and caused me to fall off balance. It dazed me. I was blurred vision. I could see him, but he picked me up, and I just went over headfirst, and knocked me out immediately. And started-- my body went into convulsions. I started flipping all over the ground. And he just kept stomping on my head, and kicking me in the head, and kicking me in the ear. Blood came out of my ears, and my nose, and everything.
<v Jared>我说，怎么回事？但他跟在我后面进来，几乎只是撞进墙里，导致我失去平衡摔倒。我头晕眼花。我视线模糊。我能看见他，但他捡起我，我只是头朝下翻过去，立刻把我撞晕了。并开始——我的身体开始抽搐。我开始在地上翻来翻去。他只是不停地跺我的头，踢我的头，踢我的耳朵。血从我的耳朵、我的鼻子，和其他地方流出来。

00:49:32.830 --> 00:49:48.110
<v Jared>He was trying to kill me. Point blank. What other excuse is there? I got seven fractures to the skull and and a concussion, lost 20% of the hearing in my right ear. I live with a headache pretty much all the time. I get pretty bad headaches.
<v Jared>他想杀我。明目张胆地。还有什么借口？我的颅骨骨折了七处，还有脑震荡，右耳听力丧失了20%。我一直带着头痛生活。我的头痛相当厉害。

00:49:48.110 --> 00:50:00.980
<v Jon  Ronson>Jared said the parents took over after that. Alex's father, a dentist, offered to pay Jared's medical bills, including a $10,000 neurologist's bill. But there was a condition.
<v Jon  Ronson>Jared说在那之后父母接管了。Alex的父亲，一名牙医，提出要支付Jared的医疗费，包括一张10,000美元的神经科医生账单。但有一个条件。

00:50:00.980 --> 00:50:08.180
<v Jared>Y'all just don't jump on Alex. Just leave him alone. I'll pay all the bills. So I just left him alone.
<v Jared>你们都不要找Alex的麻烦。只是别管他。我会付所有的账单。所以我只是别管他。

00:50:08.180 --> 00:50:21.820
<v Jon  Ronson>Jared said Alex's father also gave Jared's parents a book about why it's wrong for people to sue people. Lots of people remember Alex beating Jared up. Here's Coach Randy, who broke up the fight.
<v Jon  Ronson>Jared说Alex的父亲还给了Jared的父母一本关于为什么人们起诉别人是错误的书。很多人记得Alex打Jared。这是Randy教练，他制止了那场打斗。

00:50:21.820 --> 00:50:28.090
<v Randall Talley>Oh, golly. Alex had him upside-down. Do you know what a pile driver is?
<v Randall Talley>哦，天哪。Alex把他倒挂着。你知道什么是打桩机吗？

00:50:28.090 --> 00:50:29.530
<v Lina Misitzis>No. What is it?
<v Lina Misitzis>不。那是什么？

00:50:29.530 --> 00:50:41.950
<v Randall Talley>You literally have the person with his feet up in the air, and his head down between your legs. And you just drop to the ground, and the first thing that hits is your butt and his head at the same time.
<v Randall Talley>你确实有人的脚在空中，头在你双腿之间。你只是掉到地上，第一件事撞到的是你的屁股和他的头同时撞到。

00:50:41.950 --> 00:50:43.780
<v Lina Misitzis>Holy shit.
<v Lina Misitzis>该死的。

00:50:43.780 --> 00:50:51.730
<v Randall Talley>Yeah. Holy shit.
<v Randall Talley>是的。该死的。

00:50:51.730 --> 00:51:12.470
<v Jon  Ronson>Jared eventually returned to school. And then, one night, he was at a party. It wasn't in a barn. It was at a house, but this was the origin story that Josh the cameraman had told me. The beating in the countryside. Jared said the instigators were his friends, Mark and Brian.
<v Jon  Ronson>Jared最终回到了学校。然后，一天晚上，他在参加一个聚会。那不是在谷仓里。那是在一个房子里，但这就是摄像师Josh告诉我的起源故事。在乡村的殴打。Jared说煽动者是他的朋友Mark和Brian。

00:51:12.470 --> 00:51:20.490
<v Jon Ronson>The two guys who brought him to the party, did they know that they were taking him somewhere where he might get attacked?
<v Jon Ronson>带他去参加聚会的那两个人，他们知道他们带他去了一个可能遭到攻击的地方吗？

00:51:20.490 --> 00:51:32.500
<v Jared>The other two guys that brought him? Yeah, they loved fighting. It's all they did. They fought all the time. They figured that me or somebody would whup him. They wanted to see it, so they brought him out there.
<v Jared>带他去的那另外两个家伙？是的，他们喜欢打架。那是他们所做的一切。他们一直打架。他们认为我和别人会痛揍他。他们想看，所以他们把他带到那里。

00:51:32.500 --> 00:51:46.780
<v Jared>And he come in, he's been drinking, and just hooping and hollering, and carrying on. Finally, one of my buddies slapped him in the back of his hat. And I was trying not to even look at him, you know? He thought it was me, and there we go.
<v Jared>他进来了，他一直在喝酒，只是在那儿喊叫，坚持下去。最后，我的一个哥们儿扇了他的帽后。我试图甚至不看他，你知道吗？他以为是我，然后我们就开始了。

00:51:46.780 --> 00:52:11.170
<v Jared>He just pointed me out. He just picked me and said, "Come on. I'm gonna beat your ass like I did before." You know? He started all that flipping around, and flopping around the living room, and throwing his coat, throwing his hat. Saying he's the devil, he's Satan, and he's gonna kill me. I had to. It just was ridiculous that he was able-- that he did what he did to me. I had to prove to myself, and all my friends, hey, man, this was a fluke deal, man. You know?
<v Jared>他只是指出我。他只是挑了我，说，“来吧。我会像之前那样痛揍你。”你知道吗？他开始在那儿翻来翻去，在地板上翻来翻去，扔他的外套，扔他的帽子。说他是魔鬼，他是撒旦，他要杀我。我必须这样做。他能做到——他对我做的事太荒谬了。我必须向我自己，和所有的朋友证明，嘿，伙计，这是个侥幸的事，伙计。你知道吗？

00:52:11.170 --> 00:52:23.770
<v Jared>When I jumped on him, I hit him until I broke both my knuckles, my hands, until I couldn't hit him no more. I just reached over and grabbed this rake, this wooden handle-- steel rake, but wooden handle-- and I just thought I'd hit him in the back of the head with it.
<v Jared>当我扑向他时，我打他直到我打断了我两个指关节，我的手，直到我不能再打他。我只是伸手抓过这个耙子，这个木柄——钢耙子，但木柄——我只是想用它打他的后脑勺。

00:52:23.770 --> 00:52:41.740
<v Jared>And it knocked him down, and when he come back up running, that's when he ran into my buddy, and that was a mistake. My buddy grabbed him by the ears and planted his knee in his face. And he just took off running. And I think two or three weeks later, they moved.
<v Jared>它把他打倒了，当他再次跑起来时，那是他撞进我哥们儿怀里的时候，那是个错误。我的哥们儿抓住他的耳朵，把他的膝盖种在他的脸上。然后他就开始跑了。我想两三周后，他们搬家了。

00:52:41.740 --> 00:52:44.640
<v Jon Ronson>So they moved because of this fight?
<v Jon Ronson>所以他们因为这场打斗搬家了？

00:52:44.640 --> 00:52:45.880
<v Jared>Mm-hm.
<v Jared>嗯嗯。

00:52:45.880 --> 00:52:53.640
<v Jon Ronson>Because the Rolling Stone article said that he had uncovered some corruption in the Rockwall police force, and that's why they moved.
<v Jon Ronson>因为《滚石》文章说他揭露了Rockwall警察部队的一些腐败，那就是他们搬家的原因。

00:52:53.640 --> 00:53:09.020
<v Jared>Yeah. No, it was definitely nothing like that. They couldn't go nowhere anymore. Nowhere to go, nobody to hang out with. Nobody just couldn't stomach him. So he knew there was nothing left there in Rockwall for him.
<v Jared>是的。不，绝对没有那回事。他们不能再到任何地方去了。无处可去，没人可以出去玩。没人只是受不了他。所以他知道Rockwall对他来说已经什么都没剩了。

00:53:09.020 --> 00:53:33.180
<v Jon  Ronson>So Josh the cameraman's story had turned out to be sort of right. But he was wrong about a couple of things. It wasn't a barn. It was a house. But more importantly, the way Josh told it, the fight was the thing that had made Alex a conspiracy theorist. But Jared said, no, that's not true. He said Alex always had his theories, even before then.
<v Jon  Ronson>所以摄像师Josh的故事结果证明是某种程度上的正确。但他关于几件事是错的。那不是谷仓。那是一所房子。但更重要的是，Josh讲述它的方式，打斗是让Alex成为阴谋论者的原因。但Jared说，不，那不是真的。他说Alex在那之前就有了他的理论。

00:53:33.180 --> 00:53:57.600
<v Jared>Yeah, he had something to say about the principal, and the teachers, and the school cop, and everybody's doing all this. If we were at the pool hall, it was the guy that owned the pool hall. And he'd done called the DEA, and they were setting a deal up. It was weird, man. Everybody was like, what?
<v Jared>是的，他关于校长、老师、学校警察和每个人都在做这一切有话要说。如果我们是在台球室，那是拥有台球室的家伙。他已经叫了DEA，他们正在设置一个交易。这很奇怪，伙计。每个人都在说，什么？

00:53:57.600 --> 00:54:05.820
<v Alex Jones>Hey, guys. I'm sorry I'm, like, five minutes late. I was stuck getting back to the office. I got a lot of crazy stuff going on. It's good to be here with you guys.
<v Alex Jones>嘿，伙计们。我很抱歉，我迟到了五分钟。我被困在回办公室的路上。我有很多疯狂的事情正在进行。能和你们在一起很高兴。

00:54:05.820 --> 00:54:34.090
<v Jon  Ronson>It's a Thursday in February. Alex is talking to me from his studio in Austin. I'm at home in New York. I think the crazy stuff Alex is referring to, by the way, is that a judge has just ordered him to give a sworn deposition in the court case brought against him by some Sandy Hook parents. Alex had one condition for doing this interview. He wanted to make a brief statement. Though my story isn't about Sandy Hook, this is what he wants to say.
<v Jon  Ronson>这是二月的一个星期四。Alex正在Austin的演播室和我交谈。我在纽约家里。我想Alex指的疯狂的事情，顺便说一句，是一位法官刚刚命令他参加由桑迪胡克父母对他提起的法院案件的宣誓证词。Alex做这个采访有一个条件。他想做一个简短的声明。虽然我的故事不是关于桑迪胡克，这就是他想说的。

00:54:34.090 --> 00:54:45.330
<v Alex Jones>So here's my Sandy Hook statement. Looking back, before I was ever sued, years ago, I reviewed the information, and I do believe the horror of Sandy Hook happened.
<v Alex Jones>所以这是我的桑迪胡克声明。回顾过去，在我被起诉之前，几年前，我审查了信息，我确实相信桑迪胡克的恐怖发生了。

00:54:45.330 --> 00:54:59.560
<v Jon  Ronson>By the way, that's only sort of true. Even after Alex first admitted that children died at Sandy Hook, he hedged, saying "they probably died," and "I tend to believe they died."
<v Jon  Ronson>顺便说一句，那只在某种程度上是真的。即使Alex第一次承认孩子们死在桑迪胡克，他也避重就轻，说“他们可能死了”，并且“我倾向于相信他们死了”。

00:54:59.560 --> 00:55:07.200
<v Alex Jones>I have apologized to the families many times in the last few years if my reporting has caused them any pain.
<v Alex Jones>如果我的报道给他们造成了任何痛苦，我在过去几年里已经多次向这些家庭道歉。

00:55:07.200 --> 00:55:14.340
<v Jon  Ronson>These apologies are contentious, because he's apologized, but then continued to cast doubt on the shootings.
<v Jon  Ronson>这些道歉是有争议的，因为他道歉了，但后来继续对枪击事件表示怀疑。

00:55:14.340 --> 00:55:21.450
<v Alex Jones>I never said that anyone should harass the victims' families. And I asked the media to please stop saying that I have said that.
<v Alex Jones>我从来没有说过任何人应该骚扰受害者的家庭。我要求媒体请停止说我那样说过。

00:55:21.450 --> 00:55:39.220
<v Jon  Ronson>As best as we can tell, Alex never directly instructed his fans to harass the families. But on his broadcasts, he repeatedly talked about Lenny Pozner's ex-wife and son. And he gave Pozner's mailing address, and showed Google Earth shots of the building, and said he would probably have to go there himself.
<v Jon  Ronson>据我们所能判断，Alex从来没有直接指示他的粉丝骚扰家庭。但在他的广播中，他反复谈到了Lenny Pozner的前妻和儿子。他给了Pozner的邮寄地址，并展示了该建筑的谷歌地球镜头，并说他可能必须亲自去那里。

00:55:39.220 --> 00:55:56.870
<v Alex Jones>I ask anyone else who is going to harass the families to stop. What happened at Sandy Hook and similar events is a tragedy that needs to be recognized. It's time for us to come together as Americans, and as humans, and defend the lives of children and other defenseless individuals. Period.
<v Alex Jones>我要求任何其他将骚扰这些家庭的人停止。桑迪胡克和类似事件发生的是需要被承认的悲剧。现在是我们作为美国人，和人类团结起来，保卫孩子和其他无助个人的生命的时候了。句号。

00:55:56.870 --> 00:56:03.580
<v Jon  Ronson>Alex declined to answer follow-up questions about Sandy Hook. I got to the business at hand.
<v Jon  Ronson>Alex拒绝回答关于桑迪胡克的后续问题。我手头还有事。

00:56:03.580 --> 00:56:11.470
<v Jon Ronson>OK, so there's a guy in Rockwall called Jared, but I think you knew him maybe as Bubba.
<v Jon Ronson>好的，所以Rockwall有个叫Jared的家伙，但我认为你可能把他当作Bubba认识。

00:56:11.470 --> 00:56:25.460
<v Alex Jones>Oh. Oh, I remember Bubba, who was a senior, and I was, like, a freshman, coming and getting me out of class. And he was, like, a hall monitor, so he could do it. And then he attacked me in the hall, so I defended myself. And I'm sad that he got put in a coma, but that's just what happened.
<v Alex Jones>哦。哦，我记得Bubba，他是一个高三学生，我像个高一新生，来到这里让我离开课堂。他是个大厅监视员，所以他能做到。然后他在大厅攻击我，所以我捍卫了我自己。我很难过他陷入了昏迷，但这就是发生的事。

00:56:25.460 --> 00:56:31.530
<v Alex Jones>I've never talked about this stuff, and I'm not particularly proud of it, but I always defended myself. I never started fights.
<v Alex Jones>我从来没谈论过这些事，我不特别为它感到骄傲，但我总是捍卫我自己。我从不发起打斗。

00:56:31.530 --> 00:56:44.670
<v Jon  Ronson>This is different to Jared's version, by the way. In Jared's account, Alex started the fight. Also, Jared said he wasn't in a coma, but he was hospitalized for multiple skull fractures.
<v Jon  Ronson>顺便说一句，这和Jared的版本不同。在Jared的叙述中，Alex发起了打斗。此外，Jared说他没有昏迷，但他因为多处颅骨骨折住院。

00:56:44.670 --> 00:56:49.680
<v Jon Ronson>Jared said that he thought that you were trying to kill him.
<v Jon Ronson>Jared说他认为你试图杀他。

00:56:49.680 --> 00:57:09.280
<v Alex Jones>Well, when a 250 pound-- he would be a self-described redneck, and you weigh 160 pounds, starts attacking you, you defend yourself. So the way it works in America is, when someone physically attacks you, and you defend yourself, you're not the bad guy.
<v Alex Jones>嗯，当一个250磅的——他会是自称的乡巴佬，而你重160磅，开始攻击你时，你捍卫你自己。所以在美国运作的方式是，当某人身体上攻击你，而你捍卫你自己，你不是坏人。

00:57:09.280 --> 00:57:20.490
<v Jon  Ronson>By the way, Alex does confirm parts of Jared's story. He remembers his father paying the medical bills, though he doesn't recall a book about why it's wrong for people to sue people.
<v Jon  Ronson>顺便说一句，Alex确实证实了Jared故事的部分内容。他记得他父亲支付了医疗费，尽管他不记得一本关于为什么人们起诉别人是错误的书。

00:57:20.490 --> 00:57:31.710
<v Alex Jones>I felt real bad. My dad went and visited him at the hospital. I mean, we weren't happy about it. And I mean, that's the story you've got? What about the time-- I mean, you didn't hear about the time, like, 20 people attacked me?
<v Alex Jones>我感到非常难过。我爸爸去医院看望了他。我的意思是，我们对此并不高兴。而我的意思是，这是你拥有的故事？那次怎么样——我的意思是，你没听说过那次，比如，20个人攻击我？

00:57:31.710 --> 00:57:46.550
<v Jon Ronson>Well, the other story I heard was you were at a party, and some of Jared's friends attacked you. So was that the story that you mean?
<v Jon Ronson>嗯，我听到的另一个故事是你当时参加一个聚会，Jared的一些朋友攻击了你。那是你的意思的故事吗？

00:57:46.550 --> 00:57:50.180
<v Alex Jones>No, that never happened. So what supposedly happened at that?
<v Alex Jones>不，那从来没有发生过。那据称在那发生了什么？

00:57:50.180 --> 00:58:00.430
<v Jon Ronson>The story I heard is this. It all started with Jared, with the geography, and then you were at a party, and some of Jared's--
<v Jon Ronson>我听到的故事是这样的。这一切始于Jared，地理课，然后你在参加一个聚会，Jared的一些——

00:58:00.430 --> 00:58:04.080
<v Jon  Ronson>I told Alex everything Jared had said about the ambush.
<v Jon  Ronson>我告诉Alex关于埋伏的一切Jared说的事情。

00:58:04.080 --> 00:58:10.000
<v Jon Ronson>And that's why you left town, was because of that party. That's the story that I heard.
<v Jon Ronson>这就是为什么你离开城镇，是因为那个聚会。这是我听到的故事。

00:58:10.000 --> 00:58:29.830
<v Alex Jones>Total, complete horse crap. Total Shakespearean fiction. So what happened is, I wasn't that big of a guy, and everybody would start fights with me. I mean, this is just total fiction, totally made up. You didn't hear the part where the captain of the football team attacked me in the lunchroom, and I literally took on the entire senior football team?
<v Alex Jones>完全、彻底的马屁。完全的莎士比亚式虚构。所以发生的是，我不是那么大的家伙，每个人都会开始跟我打架。我的意思是，这完全是虚构，完全编造的。你没听到足球队长在午餐室攻击我，我真的承担了整个高级足球队的部分吗？

00:58:29.830 --> 00:58:32.440
<v Jon Ronson>No, I did not hear that.
<v Jon Ronson>不，我没有听说过。

00:58:32.440 --> 00:58:42.790
<v Alex Jones>That was an epic fight. That was like Hercules. It was like Popeye. Like, pow, pow, pow. It was just, like-- it was the greatest trip of my life. I mean--
<v Alex Jones>那是一场史诗般的战斗。那就像海格力斯。那就像大力水手。就像，砰，砰，砰。它只是，像是——那是我一生中最伟大的旅行。我的意思是——

00:58:42.790 --> 00:58:58.990
<v Jon  Ronson>Later, we talked to Alex's old friend Jacob, and one of the football players, and Coach Randy, and no one remembers it this way. At best, Jacob said, Alex fought off two or three football players. Which is actually still quite impressive.
<v Jon  Ronson>后来，我们和Alex的老朋友Jacob，以及足球运动员之一，还有Randy教练谈过，没人记得是这样。充其量，Jacob说，Alex击退了两三个足球运动员。这实际上仍然令人印象深刻。

00:58:58.990 --> 00:59:08.760
<v Alex Jones>And then, like, the whole football team, the whole senior team charges me, like a phalanx. And I just-- pow, pow. I mean, it was the best. So I thought you were actually getting to that story.
<v Alex Jones>然后，就像，整个足球队，整个高级队像方阵一样冲向我。我只是——砰，砰。我的意思是，它是最好的。所以我以为你实际上在谈论那个故事。

00:59:08.760 --> 00:59:09.690
<v Jon Ronson>No.
<v Jon Ronson>不。

00:59:09.690 --> 00:59:22.300
<v Alex Jones>I mean, poor Bubba starting a fight with me, that was a minor conquest. I tell you what, if Bubba wants to have a charity, get in the ring with me today, I'll do it. He's a big old tough guy. Let's get in the ring right now.
<v Alex Jones>我的意思是，可怜的Bubba开始跟我打架，那是小征服。我告诉你，如果Bubba想有个慈善，今天在拳击台上跟我比，我会做。他是个大块头的强硬家伙。让我们现在就上台吧。

00:59:22.300 --> 00:59:25.300
<v Jon Ronson>Well, he said he has to be very careful with his skull.
<v Jon Ronson>嗯，他说他必须非常小心他的头骨。

00:59:25.300 --> 00:59:33.580
<v Alex Jones>Well, he physically attacked me. Like, Ronson, if I came up and punched you in the face, would you have a right to defend yourself?
<v Alex Jones>嗯，他身体上攻击了我。就像，Ronson，如果我走过来打你的脸，你会有权利捍卫你自己吗？

00:59:33.580 --> 00:59:38.580
<v Jon Ronson>I would have a right to defend myself. I think it's unlikely that I would defend myself, because--
<v Jon Ronson>我会有权利捍卫我自己。我认为我不大可能捍卫我自己，因为——

00:59:38.580 --> 00:59:41.680
<v Alex Jones>Here's the thing, Jon, did I ever punch you in the face?
<v Alex Jones>这是事，Jon，我曾经打过你的脸吗？

00:59:41.680 --> 00:59:43.270
<v Jon Ronson>You've never punched me, Alex.
<v Jon Ronson>你从来没打过我，Alex。

00:59:43.270 --> 00:59:46.150
<v Alex Jones>Was I ever threatening physically to you?
<v Alex Jones>我曾经对你身体上有威胁吗？

00:59:46.150 --> 00:59:48.380
<v Jon Ronson>No. Never.
<v Jon Ronson>不。从来没。

00:59:48.380 --> 00:59:53.050
<v Alex Jones>Well, let's be honest. Have I not been a big old sweetie Teddy bear?
<v Alex Jones>嗯，老实说吧。我难道不是一个大块头的可爱泰迪熊吗？

00:59:53.050 --> 00:59:56.380
<v Jon Ronson>It's true. On a personal level.
<v Jon Ronson>这是真的。在个人层面上。

00:59:56.380 --> 01:00:20.560
<v Jon  Ronson>Alex is adamant that the party did not happen. But we confirmed that it did. We talked to two people besides Jared who say that they were there. One is named Marty Bottoms. He says he personally attacked Alex. The other is Mark Milton. When he phoned my producer Lina, she was asleep. He was on his tractor, but Lina recorded it as best as she could.
<v Jon  Ronson>Alex坚称那个聚会没有发生。但我们证实了它确实发生了。我们和除了Jared之外的两个人谈过，他们说他们当时在那里。一个叫Marty Bottoms。他说他亲自攻击了Alex。另一个是Mark Milton。当他打电话给我的制作人Lina时，她睡着了。他在他的拖拉机上，但Lina尽其所能录下了它。

01:00:20.560 --> 01:00:25.750
<v Mark Milton>I'm probably gonna lose you when I drop down this rock, girl, but yeah, this is Mark Edward Milton.
<v Mark Milton>当我在那块岩石上掉下去时，我可能会失去你，女孩，但是的，这是Mark Edward Milton。

01:00:25.750 --> 01:00:32.130
<v Jon  Ronson>Mark said he remembered Alex beating Jared unconscious in geography. And then he said this.
<v Jon  Ronson>Mark说他记得Alex在地理课上把Jared打到失去知觉。然后他说这个。

01:00:32.130 --> 01:00:35.830
<v Mark Milton>We all ended up going to a party, and then some of Bubba's friends jumped him that night.
<v Mark Milton>我们最后都去参加了一个聚会，然后Bubba的一些朋友那天晚上跳向他。

01:00:35.830 --> 01:00:39.040
<v Lina Misitzis>This was at a party after Alex beat up Jared?
<v Lina Misitzis>这是Alex打Jared之后的聚会？

01:00:39.040 --> 01:00:43.360
<v Mark Milton>Yeah. Yeah, this was at Mark's house, out there in McLendon-Chisholm.
<v Mark Milton>是的。是的，这是在Mark的房子里，在McLendon-Chisholm外面。

01:00:43.360 --> 01:00:46.750
<v Lina Misitzis>So he moved to Austin after that party?
<v Lina Misitzis>所以他在那个聚会后搬到了Austin？

01:00:46.750 --> 01:00:57.700
<v Mark Milton>Yeah, they sold the condo over in Lakeside Village. And he couldn't take it from him being jumped by a couple of boys that was Bubba's friends, and he moved out of there.
<v Mark Milton>是的，他们卖掉了Lakeside Village的公寓。他不能忍受他被Bubba的几个朋友跳向，他就搬出去了。

01:00:57.700 --> 01:01:40.780
<v Jon  Ronson>This is the story Josh had told me in the hotel lobby, and that Jared told me. It's the story Alex swears is untrue. Alex's family wouldn't talk to us, so I can't say exactly why they finally moved out of Rockwall. In our interview, Alex retold the story of the school assembly, but he also named other reasons for their move. Like how his Austin-born mother was homesick, and fed up with all the fighting. In the end, what seems clear is that this fight happened, and the assembly where Alex outed the drug dealing cops probably never did.
<v Jon  Ronson>这就是Josh在酒店大堂告诉我的故事，也是Jared告诉我的。这是Alex发誓是不真实的故事。Alex的家人没和我们谈过，所以我不能确切地说他们最后为什么搬出Rockwall。在我们的采访中，Alex重述了学校集会的故事，但他还提到了他们搬家的其他原因。比如他Austin出生的母亲是如何想家的，并且受够了所有的打斗。最后，似乎清楚的是这场打斗发生了，而Alex曝光毒贩警察的集会可能从来没有发生过。

01:01:40.780 --> 01:02:18.850
<v Jon  Ronson>If I had to guess, I would say that Alex has replaced a true story, where he's humiliated at a party, with a different story where he's a hero, standing up to corrupt cops and getting beaten up for his bravery. In a way, it's same story as the one where the whole football team came at him in a phalanx. It's the character he plays on Infowars, the beleaguered hero attacked from all sides, bloodied but undaunted, and emerging the victor. It's like stories little kids tell about themselves.
<v Jon  Ronson>如果我要猜，我会说Alex用一个不同的故事替换了一个真实的故事，他在聚会上被羞辱了，他在那儿是个英雄，反抗腐败警察并因为他的勇敢被打。在某种程度上，这和整个足球队以方阵向他冲过来的故事一样。这是他在InfoWars扮演的角色，被四面八方攻击的饱经忧患的英雄，流血但未被击倒，并成为胜利者。这就像小孩子讲述关于他们自己的故事。

01:02:18.850 --> 01:02:48.770
<v Jon  Ronson>Alex disputes most of the other things that people told me about him. He says he did not pretend to be the Antichrist in high school, says he didn't roll his eyes back in his head or dye his tongue black. He says he never told a classmate how he would like to rape her. He calls all of that insane garbage. He says he doesn't punch cabinets, or rip down blinds in the office.
<v Jon  Ronson>Alex反驳了人们告诉我的关于他的大多数其他事情。他说他在高中没假装是反基督，说他没把眼睛翻到头里去或者把舌头染黑。他说他没告诉同学他想怎么强奸她。他称那所有都是疯狂的垃圾。他说他不在办公室里打柜子或撕下百叶窗。

01:02:48.770 --> 01:03:10.100
<v Jon  Ronson>During our reporting, something very strange kept happening. It happened during Lina's call with Mark, the tractor man. Mark's daughter, Chelsea, was listening on mute as he was telling Lina how he knew for certain that the police assembly story was a lie. Just then, Chelsea unmuted herself and said to her father--
<v Jon  Ronson>在我们报道期间，一些非常奇怪的事一直在发生。它发生在Lina和拖拉机男人Mark的通话期间。Mark的女儿Chelsea在静音时在听，当时他正在告诉Lina他如何确定警察集会故事是个谎言。就在那时，Chelsea取消了静音，对她的父亲说——

01:03:10.100 --> 01:03:21.290
<v Chelsea>Nobody knows what he found out about the cops, so you can't speak and say all the reason why he left Rockwall. Because he might have found out stuff that you didn't even know about.
<v Chelsea>没人知道他关于警察发现了什么，所以你不能说话说他离开Rockwall的所有原因。因为他可能发现了你甚至不知道的事情。

01:03:21.290 --> 01:03:34.980
<v Jon  Ronson>It kept happening. All these people who knew for sure that Alex had been a liar back in Rockwall. A lot of them believed that what he says on Infowars might be true. They have a reference for him, like Coach Randy.
<v Jon  Ronson>它一直在发生。所有这些确信Alex在Rockwall时是个骗子的人。他们中的很多人相信他在InfoWars上说的话可能是真的。他们对他有崇敬，像Randy教练。

01:03:34.980 --> 01:03:42.640
<v Randall Talley>I agree with so many things what he says. A lot of people just think it. Alex goes ahead and says it.
<v Randall Talley>我同意他说的很多事情。很多人只是想它。Alex继续说出来了。

01:03:42.640 --> 01:03:53.250
<v Jon  Ronson>But not Jared. Actually, Jared had somehow gone through life not realizing that Alex was a radio host. And when I brought it up, it was awkward.
<v Jon  Ronson>但不包括Jared。事实上，Jared不知怎么走过人生没意识到Alex是个电台主持人。当我提出来时，它很尴尬。

01:03:53.250 --> 01:03:58.600
<v Jon Ronson>And you know who's a fan of his now? Donald Trump.
<v Jon Ronson>你知道现在谁是他的粉丝吗？唐纳德·特朗普。

01:03:58.600 --> 01:03:58.940
<v Jared>Is he?
<v Jared>是吗？

01:03:58.940 --> 01:04:05.190
<v Jon Ronson>Yeah. Donald Trump's been on his show. He talks about what a great reputation Alex has.
<v Jon Ronson>是的。唐纳德·特朗普一直在他的节目上。他谈论Alex有着多么伟大的名声。

01:04:05.190 --> 01:04:14.630
<v Jon  Ronson>I could tell that Jared didn't want to hear that President Trump was an Alex fan. He gave me a look to say, "are you fake news?"
<v Jon  Ronson>我看得出来Jared不想听到总统特朗普是Alex的粉丝。他给了我一个眼神说，“你是假新闻吗？”

01:04:14.630 --> 01:04:20.730
<v Jared>With the media and stuff, I don't know. I mean, I don't know what to-- I don't know. I wouldn't-- I don't know to believe that or not.
<v Jared>关于媒体和那些东西，我不知道。我的意思是，我不知道该做什么——我不知道。我不会——我不知道要相信那个还是不相信。

01:04:20.730 --> 01:04:22.760
<v Jon Ronson>He likes him. They like each other.
<v Jon Ronson>他喜欢他。他们互相喜欢。

01:04:22.760 --> 01:04:23.070
<v Jared>Do they?
<v Jared>是吗？

01:04:23.070 --> 01:04:48.730
<v Jon Ronson>Yeah. It's like all of that craziness that happened at Rockwall High School, Alex and making stuff up, and now Donald Trump's a fan. The fact is, he's carried on saying all of these crazy things, but it's no longer about the school or the pool hall. Now it's about the globalists and the Muslims. People believe him now, including the president.
<v Jon Ronson>是的。就像发生在Rockwall高中的所有疯狂事件，Alex和编造事情，而现在唐纳德·特朗普是粉丝。事实是，他继续说所有这些疯狂的事情，但它不再关于学校或台球室。现在它关于全球主义者和穆斯林。人们现在相信他，包括总统。

01:04:48.730 --> 01:04:49.700
<v Jon Ronson>[SIGHS]
<v Jon Ronson>[叹气]

01:04:49.700 --> 01:05:16.830
<v Jared>I mean-- I mean, who's to say. I mean-- I mean, some of the stuff he says could be true. It could be. I mean, Obama, he could be a Muslim. He could back them up, the radical Muslims. And he could have been giving them money behind-- I mean, who knows? We don't know. I mean, we hear what they want us to hear. We see what they want us to see. I mean, anything could be anything.
<v Jared>我的意思是——我的意思是，谁说得准。我的意思是——我的意思是，他说的一些事情可能是真的。它可能是。我的意思是，奥巴马，他可能是穆斯林。他可以支持他们，激进穆斯林。他可以在背后给他们钱——我的意思是，谁知道呢？我们不知道。我的意思是，我们听到他们想让我们听到的。我们看到他们想让我们看到的。我的意思是，任何事情都可以是任何事情。

01:05:16.830 --> 01:05:36.860
<v Jon  Ronson>Jared, more than anyone, might have understood that Alex doesn't always tell the truth. But no, this is Alex's legacy, the chaos he sows in the world, the feeling that nothing can be known for sure.
<v Jon  Ronson>Jared，比任何人，可能更明白Alex并不总是说实话。但不，这是Alex的遗产，他在世界上播下的混乱，没有任何事情可以确切知道的感觉。

01:05:36.860 --> 01:06:21.440
<v Ira Glass>Jon Ronson. He and his, producer Lina Misitzis, originally created a version of this story for audible.com, where they also did Jon's latest long form original for Audible, The Last Days of August, a deep dive into the never before told story of what caused the untimely death of 23-year-old porn star August Ames. It's available exclusively on audible.com. Audible is the world's largest producer and provider of downloadable audio books and other spoken word entertainment.
<v Ira Glass>Jon Ronson。他和他的，制作人Lina Misitzis，最初为audible.com创建了这个故事的一个版本，他们也在那儿为Audible做了Jon最新的长篇原创，August的最后日子，关于是什么导致23岁的色情明星August Ames英年早逝的从未被讲述过的故事的深度挖掘。它在audible.com独家提供。Audible是世界上最大的可下载有声读物和其他口述娱乐的制作商和提供商。

01:06:21.440 --> 01:06:36.140
<v Ira Glass>Our program was produced today by Dana Chivvis. The people who put our show together today includes Ben Calhoun, Sean Cole, Aviva DeKornfeld, Damien Graef, Michelle Harris, Miki Meek, Stowe Nelson, Catherine Raimondo, Ben Phelan, Nadia Reiman, Robyn Semien, Lilly Sullivan, Christopher Swetala, Matt Tierney, Julie Whitaker, and Diane Wu.
<v Ira Glass>我们的节目今天由Dana Chivvis制作。今天组装我们节目的人包括Ben Calhoun, Sean Cole, Aviva DeKornfeld, Damien Graef, Michelle Harris, Miki Meek, Stowe Nelson, Catherine Raimondo, Ben Phelan, Nadia Reiman, Robyn Semien, Lilly Sullivan, Christopher Swetala, Matt Tierney, Julie Whitaker, 和 Diane Wu。

01:06:36.140 --> 01:06:49.250
<v Ira Glass>Our managing editor is David Kestenbaum. Special thanks today to Sandy and Lonnie Phillips, Whitney Phillips, Dr. Kenneth Henderson, Joel Ronson, Elizabeth Scholer, David Bloom, Jonathan Kerlan, Sophia Hillsman, and Eric Newsom.
<v Ira Glass>我们的执行编辑是David Kestenbaum。今天特别感谢Sandy和Lonnie Phillips, Whitney Phillips, Kenneth Henderson博士, Joel Ronson, Elizabeth Scholer, David Bloom, Jonathan Kerlan, Sophia Hillsman, 和 Eric Newsom。

